| width = 33%
}}

On 21 November, Lewandowski scored a hat-trick against [[S.L. Benfica|Benfica]] in a [[2021–22 UEFA Champions League#Group stage|Champions League group stage]] match, becoming the fastest player to 80 UCL goals, in 100 appearances, edging past the previous record of [[Lionel Messi]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Samji |first=Mitul |date=4 November 2021 |title=Lewandowski beats Messi and Ronaldo goalscoring record with hat-trick in 100th CL game |url=https://talksport.com/football/974728/robert-lewandowski-lionel-messi-cristiano-ronaldo-goal-record-champions-league/ |access-date=24 January 2024 |website=talkSPORT |archive-date=24 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240124190214/https://talksport.com/football/974728/robert-lewandowski-lionel-messi-cristiano-ronaldo-goal-record-champions-league/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last= |date=28 November 2023 |title=Champions League goalscoring milestones: Haaland quickest to 40 |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/027d-170b3182d9ed-587169daf860-1000--champions-league-goalscoring-milestones-haaland-quickest-/ |access-date=24 January 2024 |publisher=[[UEFA]] |language=en |archive-date=24 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240124190214/https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/027d-170b3182d9ed-587169daf860-1000--champions-league-goalscoring-milestones-haaland-quickest-/ |url-status=live }}</ref> On 23 November, he opened the score with a [[bicycle kick]] in a 2–1 away win against [[FC Dynamo Kyiv|Dynamo Kyiv]] in a [[2021–22 UEFA Champions League#Group stage|Champions League group stage]] match, thereby becoming the first player to score in nine consecutive games in two separate seasons of the competition.<ref>{{Cite web|date=23 November 2021|title=Lewandowski sets another record as he scores stunning overhead kick with shoe untied|url=https://talksport.com/football/988561/robert-lewandowski-overhead-kick-bayern-munich-champions-league/|access-date=25 November 2021|website=talkSPORT|archive-date=24 November 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211124082720/https://talksport.com/football/988561/robert-lewandowski-overhead-kick-bayern-munich-champions-league/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Badshah |first=Nadeem |date=23 November 2021 |title=CHAMPIONS LEAGUE RESULT - ROBERT LEWANDOWSKI AND KINGSLEY COMAN ON TARGET AS BAYERN MUNICH BEAT DYNAMO KYIV |url=https://www.tntsports.co.uk/football/champions-league/2021-2022/dynamo-kyiv-v-bayern-munich-follow-live-coverage_sto8637933/story.shtml?welcome=eurosport |access-date=23 January 2024 |website=eurosport.com |archive-date=24 August 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250824094752/https://www.tntsports.co.uk/football/champions-league/2021-2022/dynamo-kyiv-v-bayern-munich-follow-live-coverage_sto8637933/story.shtml?welcome=eurosport |url-status=live }}</ref> Midway through the season, Lewandowski finished second in the [[2021 Ballon d'Or]] award, behind Lionel Messi of Paris Saint-Germain and received the [[2021 Ballon d'Or|Striker of the Year]] award by the ''[[France Football]]'' magazine.<ref name="Best Striker">{{Cite news|last=Murray|first=Scott|date=29 November 2021|title=Ballon d'Or 2021 – live updates!|work=The Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/live/2021/nov/29/ballon-dor-2021-live-updates|access-date=29 November 2021|issn=0261-3077|archive-date=29 November 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211129183917/https://www.theguardian.com/football/live/2021/nov/29/ballon-dor-2021-live-updates|url-status=live}}</ref> On 17 December, Lewandowski set the Bundesliga record for most goals in a calendar year with his 43rd goal.<ref>{{cite web|title=Mueller scores in 400th game as Bayern crush Wolfsburg|url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/report?gameId=608685|publisher=[[ESPN]]|date=17 December 2021|access-date=17 December 2021|archive-date=17 December 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211217214247/https://www.espn.com/soccer/report?gameId=608685|url-status=live}}</ref> He became the second player, after [[Cristiano Ronaldo]], to be the top goalscorer for club and country as a player playing in Europe for three consecutive years.<ref name=":5">{{cite news |date=30 December 2021 |title=Lewandowski, Mbappé, Ronaldo: Who was the top scorer in 2021? |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/0270-141002a443bb-91ed70c115b8-1000--lewandowski-mbappe-ronaldo-who-was-the-top-scorer-in-2021/ |access-date=23 January 2024 |publisher=[[UEFA]] |archive-date=23 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240123002432/https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/0270-141002a443bb-91ed70c115b8-1000--lewandowski-mbappe-ronaldo-who-was-the-top-scorer-in-2021/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name=":6">{{cite web |last=Shukla |first=Rajarshi |date=9 January 2023 |title=Who has been the top scorer each year since turn of the millennium? |url=https://khelnow.com/football/2023-01-world-football-top-scorer-each-year-since-turn-of-millennium |access-date=23 January 2024 |website=Khel Now |archive-date=23 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240123002434/https://khelnow.com/football/2023-01-world-football-top-scorer-each-year-since-turn-of-millennium |url-status=live }}</ref> His 69 goals in 59 games for club and country in 2021 matched Cristiano Ronaldo's best overall scoring year of 69 goals in 59 games for club and country in 2013.<ref name=":6" />

On 15 January 2022, Lewandowski scored his 16th hat-trick and 300th Bundesliga goal in a 4–0 away win over Köln.<ref>{{cite web |title=Lewandowski scores 300th Bundesliga goal as Bayern rout Cologne |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/60008495 |work=BBC Sport |date=15 January 2022 |access-date=16 January 2022 |archive-date=15 January 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220115180652/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/60008495 |url-status=live }}</ref> On 16 February 2022, in a match against [[FC Red Bull Salzburg|Red Bull Salzburg]] that ended in a draw of 1–1, Lewandowski's record streak of 22 consecutive winning Champions League matches ended.<ref>{{Cite web |date=18 February 2022 |title=RECORD WINNING SERIE ENDED ! |url=https://iffhs.com/en/news/record-winning-serie-ended-1694 |access-date=26 June 2026 |publisher=[[IFFHS]] |archive-date=20 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240420101225/https://www.iffhs.com/posts/1694 |url-status=live }}</ref> On 8 March, Lewandowski scored a hat-trick in a 7–1 win over [[FC Red Bull Salzburg|Red Bull Salzburg]] in the second leg of [[2021–22 UEFA Champions League knockout phase#Round of 16|Champions League round of 16]]. Coming inside the first 23 minutes of the match, Lewandowski's hat-trick becomes the earliest ever scored by a player from the start of a Champions League match.<ref name=":3">{{Cite web |last=Wright |first=Chris |date=9 March 2022 |title=How Lewandowski's 11-minute hat trick ranks in the all-time UCL list |url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/37626160/lewandowski-smashes-champions-league-hat-trick-records-win-salzburg |access-date=23 January 2024 |publisher=[[ESPN]] |language=en |archive-date=23 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240123035551/https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/37626160/lewandowski-smashes-champions-league-hat-trick-records-win-salzburg |url-status=live }}</ref> Taking just 11 minutes from first goal to last, Lewandowski's three-goal extravaganza against Salzburg also ranks as the quickest hat-trick ever scored in the knockout phases of the Champions League.<ref name=":3" /> With these goals he took himself beyond the 40-goal mark in all competitions for the seventh consecutive season.<ref>{{Cite web |date=9 March 2022 |title=Lewandowski smashes Champions League hat trick records in win over Salzburg |url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/37626160/lewandowski-smashes-champions-league-hat-trick-records-win-salzburg |publisher=ESPN |access-date=11 March 2022 |archive-date=29 July 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220729095015/https://www.espn.com/soccer/blog-the-toe-poke/story/4612704/lewandowski-smashes-champions-league-hat-trick-records-in-win-over-salzburg |url-status=live }}</ref> With the hat-trick, he also became the fastest player to 85 UCL goals, again edging past Lionel Messi's previous record.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Oyeleke |first=Sodiq |date=8 March 2022 |title=Lewandowski breaks record, scores fastest Champions League hat-trick |url=https://punchng.com/lewandowski-breaks-record-scores-fastest-champions-league-hat-trick/ |access-date=24 January 2024 |newspaper=[[The Punch]] |language=en-US |archive-date=24 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240124190843/https://punchng.com/lewandowski-breaks-record-scores-fastest-champions-league-hat-trick/ |url-status=live }}</ref> He also joined [[Cristiano Ronaldo]] and Messi as the only three players to have ten or more goals in three or more UCL campaigns, and joined Messi as the only two players who have scored a first half hat trick in a UCL knockout game.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Menon |first=Anirudh |date=10 March 2022 |title=UCL stats: Benzema's unique first, Lewandowski joins Ronaldo, Messi |url=https://www.espn.co.uk/football/story/_/id/37626187/ucl-stats-benzemas-unique-first-lewandowski-joins-ronaldo-messi |access-date=24 January 2024 |publisher=[[ESPN]] |language=en |archive-date=24 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240124191731/https://www.espn.co.uk/football/story/_/id/37626187/ucl-stats-benzemas-unique-first-lewandowski-joins-ronaldo-messi |url-status=live }}</ref> However, Lewandowski finished the league with 35 goals as top scorer for the fifth consecutive season and seventh outright, equaling the record of Gerd Müller. He also broke the Bundesliga record for most away goals in a single season with 19 goals.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/robert-lewandowski-wins-2021-22-bundesliga-top-scorer-bayern-munich-19935 |title=Robert Lewandowski wins 2021/22 Bundesliga top scorer's cannon |website=Bundesliga |date=14 May 2022 |access-date=14 May 2022 |archive-date=22 September 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220922004912/https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/robert-lewandowski-wins-2021-22-bundesliga-top-scorer-bayern-munich-19935 |url-status=live }}</ref> In addition, he won his second European Golden Shoe award for the second consecutive season.<ref name="neogol">{{cite web |url=https://www.neogol.com/clasificacion-bota-de-oro/ |title=Clasificación Bota de Oro 2022. ¡Actualizada! |website=neogol.com |language=es |date=22 May 2022 |access-date=22 May 2022 |archive-date=31 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220831203209/https://www.neogol.com/clasificacion-bota-de-oro/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 30 May 2022, Lewandowski stated his desire to leave Bayern Munich, saying "My story with Bayern has come to an end, I cannot imagine further good cooperation... I hope they will not stop me (from leaving) just because they can. A transfer is the best solution for everyone."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Whitehead |first=Jacob |title=Lewandowski admits Bayern story 'at end' |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/4176541/2022/05/30/robert-lewandowski-my-bayern-munich-story-has-come-to-an-end/ |access-date=30 May 2022 |website=The Athletic |language=en |archive-date=25 June 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220625051647/https://theathletic.com/news/robert-lewandowski-my-bayern-story-at-end/GTLY1OxvUrWo/ |url-status=live }}</ref> A year before his departure, Bayern Munich explored the possibility of signing [[Erling Haaland]] from Borussia Dortmund as a potential successor to Lewandowski. According to Sebastian Staszewski's biography ''Lewandowski. Prawdziwy'', Lewandowski and his agent Pini Zahavi became aware of Bayern's interest despite [[Hasan Salihamidžić]]'s reported denial, which allegedly affected Lewandowski's relationship with the club.<ref>{{cite web |last=Blöding |first=Falko |url=https://www.goal.com/de/listen/ohne-mit-der-wimper-zu-zucken-ex-bayern-boss-hasan-salihamidzic-belog-robert-lewandowski-wegen-erling-haaland/bltbc06756fac9657d7 |title=Ohne mit der Wimper zu zucken! Ex-Bayern-Boss Hasan Salihamidzic belog Robert Lewandowski wegen Erling Haaland |publisher=Goal.com |language=de |date=11 July 2026 |access-date=11 July 2026 |archive-date=13 July 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260713032346/https://www.goal.com/de/listen/ohne-mit-der-wimper-zu-zucken-ex-bayern-boss-hasan-salihamidzic-belog-robert-lewandowski-wegen-erling-haaland/bltbc06756fac9657d7 |url-status=live }}</ref> Haaland later revealed that he had sympathized with Lewandowski, describing the situation as "disrespectful" given his achievements at Bayern.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://sport.sky.de/fussball/artikel/manchester-city-haaland-spricht-ueber-lewandowski-und-bayern-muenchen/12688482/34946 |title=Manchester City: Haaland spricht über Lewandowski und Bayern München |publisher=Sky Sport |language=de |date=3 September 2022 |access-date=11 July 2026 |archive-date=3 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221203122657/https://sport.sky.de/fussball/artikel/manchester-city-haaland-spricht-ueber-lewandowski-und-bayern-muenchen/12688482/34946 |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Barcelona===

====Transfer====
At Bayern Munich, Lewandowski established himself as one of the best players of his generation. On 16 July 2022, [[FC Barcelona|Barcelona]] confirmed they had reached an agreement with Bayern Munich for Lewandowski's transfer.<ref>f{{cite web|url=https://www.fcbarcelona.es/es/football/first-team/news/2680144/principle-of-agreement-for-the-transfer-of-lewandowski|title=Principle of agreement for the transfer of Lewandowski|date=16 July 2022|access-date=19 July 2022|publisher=[[FC Barcelona]]|archive-date=15 November 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221115044026/https://www.fcbarcelona.es/es/football/first-team/news/2680144/principle-of-agreement-for-the-transfer-of-lewandowski|url-status=live}}</ref> Three days later, Lewandowski signed a four-year contract for a fee of €45&nbsp;million, potentially rising to €50&nbsp;million with add-ons.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fcbarcelona.com/en/football/first-team/news/2683853/agreement-with-bayern-munich-for-the-transfer-of-robert-lewandowski |title=Agreement with Bayern Munich for the transfer of Robert Lewandowski |publisher=FC Barcelona |date=19 July 2022 |access-date=19 July 2022 |archive-date=23 July 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220723133600/https://www.fcbarcelona.com/en/football/first-team/news/2683853/agreement-with-bayern-munich-for-the-transfer-of-robert-lewandowski |url-status=live }}</ref> The contract included a [[Buyout clause|release clause]] set at €500 million.<ref>{{Cite web |date=19 July 2022 |title=Lewandowski completes Barca move from Bayern |url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/37630151/robert-lewandowski-completes-barcelona-move-bayern-munich |access-date=20 July 2022 |publisher=[[ESPN]] |language=en |archive-date=22 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221022000528/https://www.espn.com/soccer/soccer-transfers/story/4701830/robert-lewandowski-completes-barcelona-move-from-bayern-munich |url-status=live }}</ref> Lewandowski became the most expensive Polish player in history and Bayern Munich's most expensive sale of all time.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://sport.tvp.pl/61317657/robert-lewandowski-z-ostatnim-rekordem-w-bayernie-monachium-najdrozszy-transfer-wychodzacy-w-historii-klubu|title=Robert Lewandowski with the last record in Bayern Munich. The most expensive outgoing transfer in the history of the club|access-date=19 July 2022|publisher=Meczyki.pl|language=pl|archive-date=16 July 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220716044021/https://sport.tvp.pl/61317657/robert-lewandowski-z-ostatnim-rekordem-w-bayernie-monachium-najdrozszy-transfer-wychodzacy-w-historii-klubu|url-status=live}}</ref> Lewandowski was formally unveiled in front of 50,000 fans on 5 August at the [[Camp Nou]], and was handed the number 9 shirt, previously worn by [[Memphis Depay]], and was officially registered on 12 August, amid speculation that the club could not register him as they were over the league's salary cap limit, due to their financial difficulties.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.espn.cl/futbol/espana/nota/_/id/10728135/barcelona-robert-lewandowski-camp-nou-presentacion-record|title=Lewandowski lifts passions at Camp Nou in a record presentation|access-date=15 November 2022|date=5 August 2022|work=[[ESPN]]|archive-date=15 November 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221115044020/https://www.espn.cl/futbol/espana/nota/_/id/10728135/barcelona-robert-lewandowski-camp-nou-presentacion-record|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.marca.com/futbol/barcelona/2022/08/05/62ed03ed268e3e850f8b4578.html|title=Barça removes the number '9' from Memphis to give it to Lewandowski|access-date=6 August 2022|date=5 August 2022|work=[[Marca (newspaper)|Marca]]|archive-date=19 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221219175208/https://www.marca.com/futbol/barcelona/2022/08/05/62ed03ed268e3e850f8b4578.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.20minutos.es/deportes/noticia/5040615/0/barcelona-obligado-inscrito-kessie-christensen-laliga/|work=20minutes|access-date=12 August 2022|title=48 hour alert: Barça has until Saturday to sign up Kessié and Christensen or they will leave for free and without making their debut|archive-date=30 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231030215157/https://www.20minutos.es/deportes/noticia/5040615/0/barcelona-obligado-inscribir-kessie-christensen-laliga/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://as.com/futbol/primera/la-hora-limite-del-barca-para-inscrito-jugadores-este-sabado-n/ |work=[[Diario AS]] |access-date=12 August 2022 |title=Barça's deadline to register players, this Saturday }}{{Dead link|date=July 2023 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref>

====2022–23: La Liga title and Pichichi Trophy====
On 13 August, he made his competitive debut for the club in 0–0 draw against [[Rayo Vallecano]] in the league.<ref>{{Cite web |date=13 August 2022 |title=Barcelona frustrated by Rayo Vallecano as Lewandowski & Raphinha's La Liga debuts spoiled |url=https://www.goal.com/en-in/news/barcelona-frustrated-rayo-vallecano-opening-night/bltcd5e7b01eea1ab09 |access-date=16 August 2022 |language=en |archive-date=16 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220816104641/https://www.goal.com/en-in/news/barcelona-frustrated-rayo-vallecano-opening-night/bltcd5e7b01eea1ab09 |url-status=live }}</ref> On 21 August, he scored his first competitive goals for ''Blaugrana'', netting a brace in a 4–1 victory over [[Real Sociedad]] on 21 August,<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.laprensa.hn/deportes/barcelona-real-sociedad-liga-espana-espanola-anoeta-xavi-lewandowski-MC9664259|title=Lewandowski brilla con doblete en goleada del Barcelona ante la Real Sociedad|access-date=21 August 2022|work=La Prensa|archive-date=21 August 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220821170957/https://www.laprensa.hn/deportes/barcelona-real-sociedad-liga-espana-espanola-anoeta-xavi-lewandowski-MC9664259|url-status=live}}</ref> followed by another brace against [[Real Valladolid]] in a 4–0 victory on 28 August.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.latimes.com/espanol/deportes/articulo/2022-08-29/lewandowski-repeats-doblete-y-el-barca-golea-4-0-a-valladolid|title=Lewandowski repeats double and Barça thrashes Valladolid|access-date=3 September 2022|date=30 August 2022|website=[[Los Angeles Times]]|language=es-us}}{{Dead link|date=October 2023 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref> On 7 September, in his first game as a Barcelona player in [[2022–23 UEFA Champions League|Champions League]], he scored a hat-trick in a 5–1 victory over [[FC Viktoria Plzeň|Viktoria Plzeň]], becoming the first player in history to score a Champions League hat-trick for three different clubs.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/62825071 | title=Lewandowski hits hat-trick before Bayern return | access-date=8 September 2022 | archive-date=8 September 2022 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220908000856/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/62825071 | url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.soccernews.com/lewandowski-makes-champions-league-history-with-barcelona-hat-trick/342278/ | title=Lewandowski makes Champions League history with Barcelona hat-trick | access-date=8 September 2022 | archive-date=7 September 2022 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220907234342/https://www.soccernews.com/lewandowski-makes-champions-league-history-with-barcelona-hat-trick/342278/ | url-status=live }}</ref> On 11 September, he scored his sixth league goal of the season in his fifth league match for Barcelona, in their 4–0 win over [[Cádiz CF|Cádiz]], setting the record for most goals in the first five La Liga games of the season in the 21st century,<ref>{{Cite web |date=11 September 2022 |title=Lewandowski, best goalscoring start in LaLiga this century |url=https://www.fcbarcelona.com/en/news/2787865/lewandowski-best-goalscoring-start-in-laliga-this-century |access-date=25 January 2024 |publisher=FC Barcelona |archive-date=17 June 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250617070902/https://www.fcbarcelona.com/en/news/2787865/lewandowski-best-goalscoring-start-in-laliga-this-century |url-status=live }}</ref> and eventually registered eleven goal contributions including nine goals and two assists in seven matches, after scoring the only goal of an away win over [[RCD Mallorca|Mallorca]] on 1 October.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.infobae.com/america/peru/2022/10/01/gol-lewandowski-1-0-barcelona-vs-mallorca-hoy-laliga/|title=Great goal by Lewandowski for the 1-0 win between Barcelona and Mallorca for LaLiga|access-date=10 October 2022|date=1 October 2022|website=infobae|language=es-es|archive-date=14 October 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221014223317/https://www.infobae.com/america/peru/2022/10/01/gol-lewandowski-1-0-barcelona-vs-mallorca-hoy-laliga/|url-status=live}}</ref>

On 12 October, Lewandowski scored a brace in Barcelona's Champions League fixture against [[Inter Milan]], with his last-minute equalizer securing a 3–3 home draw for the Blaugrana at Camp Nou.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/63221311 |title=Barcelona 3–3 Inter Milan |publisher=BBC Sport |date=12 October 2022 |access-date=15 November 2022 |archive-date=4 November 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221104110942/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/63221311 |url-status=live }}</ref> Despite scoring five goals in the competition, his goals were not able to help Barcelona, as they finished third in the [[2022–23 UEFA Champions League group stage|group stage]] which put them in the [[UEFA Europa League|Europa League]] [[2022–23 UEFA Europa League knockout phase|knockout round play-offs]] for the second consecutive season.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.goal.com/en/news/barcelona-back-europa-league-where-they-belong-right-now/bltb94f0b887e0b4ef3 |title=Barcelona back where they belong right now: the Europa League |website=[[Goal (website)|Goal]] |date=26 October 2022 |access-date=15 November 2022 |archive-date=31 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221231085208/https://www.goal.com/en/news/barcelona-back-europa-league-where-they-belong-right-now/bltb94f0b887e0b4ef3 |url-status=live }}</ref> On 8 November, Lewandowski was sent off for the second time in his club career for a foul on [[David García (footballer, born 1994)|David García]], later receiving a three-game ban, as Barcelona won 2–1 against [[CA Osasuna|Osasuna]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2022/11/09/sport/barcelona-osasuna-pique-lewandowski-la-liga-spt-intl/index.html |title=Gerard Piqué and Robert Lewandowski sent off as Barcelona fights back to defeat Osasuna |publisher=[[CNN]] |date=9 November 2022 |access-date=9 November 2022 |archive-date=23 November 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221123004128/https://edition.cnn.com/2022/11/09/sport/barcelona-osasuna-pique-lewandowski-la-liga-spt-intl/index.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.reuters.com/lifestyle/sports/barcelonas-lewandowski-given-three-game-ban-red-card-2022-11-16/ |title=Barcelona's Lewandowski given three-game ban for red card |publisher=[[Reuters]] |date=16 November 2022 |access-date=5 January 2023 |archive-date=5 January 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230105211727/https://www.reuters.com/lifestyle/sports/barcelonas-lewandowski-given-three-game-ban-red-card-2022-11-16/ |url-status=live }}</ref> However, Lewandowski participated in the 1–1 tie against [[Derbi Barceloní|rivals]] [[RCD Espanyol|Espanyol]] on 31 December after his ban was suspended by a court in [[Madrid]], but still ended up serving the disqualification, as Spain's sports court upheld the punishment, missing the league matches against [[Atlético Madrid]], [[Girona FC|Girona]] and [[Getafe CF|Getafe]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/64168380 |title=Robert Lewandowski: Barcelona striker's three-game ban upheld |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=4 January 2023 |access-date=5 January 2023 |archive-date=4 January 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230104225927/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/64168380 |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 16 January 2023, he scored the second goal in the [[2023 Supercopa de España final]], as Barcelona defeated Real Madrid 3–1 in ''[[El Clásico]]'', winning his first title with the club.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fcbarcelona.com/en/football/first-team/news/3023483/first-trophy-of-the-xavi-era |title=First trophy of the Xavi era |work=FC Barcelona |date=15 January 2023 |access-date=5 March 2023 |archive-date=19 January 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230119013317/https://www.fcbarcelona.com/en/football/first-team/news/3023483/first-trophy-of-the-xavi-era |url-status=live }}</ref> On 14 May, he scored two goals as Barcelona defeated Espanyol 4–2, confirming them as La Liga champions.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Barcelona crowned La Liga champions after derby win |language=en-GB |work=BBC Sport |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/65590309 |access-date=14 May 2023 |archive-date=14 May 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230514210105/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/65590309 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Booth |first=Chuck |title=Barcelona clinch La Liga title over Real Madrid after bashing city rival Espanyol 4-2 |url=https://www.cbssports.com/soccer/news/barcelona-clinch-la-liga-title-over-real-madrid-after-bashing-city-rival-espanyol-4-2/ |access-date=14 May 2023 |publisher=CBS Sports |language=en |archive-date=14 May 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230514213602/https://www.cbssports.com/soccer/news/barcelona-clinch-la-liga-title-over-real-madrid-after-bashing-city-rival-espanyol-4-2/ |url-status=live }}</ref> He was the first Barcelona player to score more than 30 goals across all competitions in his debut season since [[Ronaldo (Brazilian footballer)|Ronaldo Nazário]] in [[1996–97 FC Barcelona season|1996–97]].<ref>{{cite tweet |url=https://twitter.com/Squawka/status/1657846163754582022?lang=en |title=Robert Lewandowski is the first Barcelona player to score 30+ goals across all competitions in his debut season since Ronaldo in 1996/97. |user=Squawka |author=Squawka |number=1657846163754582022 |date=14 May 2023 |access-date=30 January 2024}}</ref> By the end of the [[2022–23 La Liga]] season, Lewandowski won his first [[Pichichi Trophy]] with 23 goals in 34 matches,<ref name="pichichi1">{{cite web |url=https://www.sport.es/en/news/laliga/barcelona-striker-lewandowski-wins-pichichi-in-first-season-in-laliga-86673966 |title=Barcelona striker Lewandowski wins Pichichi in first season in LaLiga |website=[[Sport (Spanish newspaper)|Sport]] |date=4 June 2023 |access-date=4 June 2023 |archive-date=4 June 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230604214056/https://www.sport.es/en/news/laliga/barcelona-striker-lewandowski-wins-pichichi-in-first-season-in-laliga-86673966 |url-status=live }}</ref> becoming the first player in top 5 European leagues to get top scorer award in six consecutive seasons.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gokalp |first=Selcuk Bugra |date=21 June 2023 |title=Top scorers lead their teams to league titles in European leagues |url=https://www.aa.com.tr/en/europe/top-scorers-lead-their-teams-to-league-titles-in-european-leagues/2927850 |access-date=23 January 2024 |publisher=[[Anadolu Agency]] |archive-date=23 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240123032129/https://www.aa.com.tr/en/europe/top-scorers-lead-their-teams-to-league-titles-in-european-leagues/2927850 |url-status=live }}</ref> Lewandowski also tied [[Lionel Messi]] for most top scorer awards in top 5 European leagues with eight.<ref name=":4" />

====2023–24: La Liga runner-up====
[[File:Robert Lewandoski, jugador del FCBarcelona durant la gira de pretemporada a EUA. (05-08-2024) (cropped).jpg|thumb|190px|right|Lewandowski in 2024 during [[FC Barcelona|Barcelona]]'s pre-season tour in the United States]]
On 19 September 2023, Lewandowski scored once in Barcelona's 5–0 home win over [[Royal Antwerp F.C.|Antwerp]] in the first matchday of the [[2023–24 UEFA Champions League]] to bring his [[UEFA]] competitions tally to 100 goals, becoming only the [[UEFA club competition records and statistics#Top scorers in UEFA club competitions|third player]] to reach such a milestone after [[Cristiano Ronaldo]] and [[Lionel Messi]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fcbarcelona.com/en/football/first-team/news/3691389/fc-barcelona-5-0-royal-antwerp-brilliant-start |title=FC Barcelona 5–0 Royal Antwerp: Brilliant start |publisher=FC Barcelona |date=19 September 2023 |access-date=20 September 2023 |archive-date=2 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231002023026/https://www.fcbarcelona.com/en/football/first-team/news/3691389/fc-barcelona-5-0-royal-antwerp-brilliant-start |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.goal.com/en/news/lewandowski-elite-club-barcelona-volley-ronaldo-messi/blt63ebb3a442cb9ada |title=Barcelona striker Robert Lewandowski volleys home 100th European goal to join Lionel Messi and Cristiano Ronaldo in exclusive club |publisher=GOAL |date=19 September 2023 |access-date=20 September 2023 |archive-date=2 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231002023129/https://www.goal.com/en/news/lewandowski-elite-club-barcelona-volley-ronaldo-messi/blt63ebb3a442cb9ada |url-status=live }}</ref> He also became the oldest player, at 35 years and 29 days, to score for Barcelona in the UEFA Champions League, surpassing [[Gerard Piqué]]'s previous record.<ref>{{Cite web |date=20 September 2023 |title=IFFHS CONTINENTAL NEWS - UEFA CHAMPIONS LEAGUE |url=https://iffhs.com/en/news/iffhs-continental-news-uefa-champions-league-3050 |access-date=27 January 2024 |publisher=[[IFFHS]] |archive-date=19 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240519111732/https://iffhs.com/posts/3050 |url-status=live }}</ref> On 23 September, he scored a brace to help Barcelona overturn a two-goal deficit in a 3–2 home victory against [[RC Celta de Vigo|Celta Vigo]], becoming the best scorer in first 50 matches for the club in 21st century, with 35 goals, surpassing the record previously held by [[Samuel Eto'o]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ansari |first=Ahmad Sarmad |date=23 September 2023 |title=Barcelona star forward overtakes Samuel Eto'o's record with club |url=https://barcanewsnetwork.com/barcelona-star-forward-overtakes-samuel-etoos-record-with-club/ |access-date=25 January 2024 |publisher=Barca News Network |language=en-us |archive-date=25 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240125033405/https://barcanewsnetwork.com/barcelona-star-forward-overtakes-samuel-etoos-record-with-club/ |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.telecomasia.net/news/football/lewandowski-sets-barcelonaundefineds-performance-record-in-21st-century/ |title=Lewandowski Sets Barcelona's Performance Record In 21st Century |website=telecomasia.net |author=Marina Magomedova |date=24 September 2023 |access-date=24 September 2023 |archive-date=30 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231030215212/https://www.telecomasia.net/news/other/betboom-team-vs-shopify-rebellion-dreamleague-s21-final-day-schedule/?action=load-next-news |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite tweet |url=https://twitter.com/ManagingBarca/status/1705521020713717972 |title=Robert Lewandowski has scored 35 goals in his first 50 games with FC Barcelona. |user=ManagingBarca |number=1705521020713717972 |date=23 September 2023 |access-date=30 January 2024}}</ref>

On 17 February 2024, Lewandowski secured a win for Barcelona in a 2–1 victory over Celta Vigo by converting a retaken 97th-minute penalty.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/68327478 |title=Celta Vigo 1-2 Barcelona: Robert Lewandowski scores late winner |publisher=BBC Sport |date=17 February 2024 |access-date=3 March 2024 |archive-date=9 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240509073907/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/68327478 |url-status=live }}</ref> He became the most successful footballer in terms of the number of goals scored (407) over the past decade in the top five [[Big Five (association football)|major European football league]]s.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://sportowefakty.wp.pl/pilka-nozna/1109515/tak-to-prawda-lewandowski-lepszy-od-messiego-i-ronaldo |language=pl |title=Kto strzelił najwięcej goli w ostatnich 10 latach? Sprawdźcie |website=wp.pl |author=Dawid Borek |date=2 March 2024 |access-date=3 March 2024 |archive-date=13 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240413232552/https://sportowefakty.wp.pl/pilka-nozna/1109515/tak-to-prawda-lewandowski-lepszy-od-messiego-i-ronaldo |url-status=live }}</ref>
On 22 February, he scored his 93rd [[UEFA Champions League|Champions League]] goal in a 1–1 draw against [[SSC Napoli|Napoli]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.espn.in/football/report/_/gameId/691517 |title=Napoli fight back to draw with Barcelona in Champions League |publisher=ESPN |date=22 February 2024 |access-date=3 March 2024 |archive-date=3 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240303091438/https://www.espn.in/football/report/_/gameId/691517 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.pap.pl/aktualnosci/gol-lewandowskiego-w-lidze-mistrzow-podzial-punktow-w-neapolu |language=pl |title=Gol Lewandowskiego w Lidze Mistrzów. Podział punktów w Neapolu. |website=pap.pl |date=22 February 2024 |access-date=3 March 2024 |archive-date=15 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250515235950/https://www.pap.pl/aktualnosci/gol-lewandowskiego-w-lidze-mistrzow-podzial-punktow-w-neapolu |url-status=live }}</ref> Then on 12 March, Lewandowski scored the final goal in a 3–1 win in the home leg, knocking out Napoli with a 4–2 aggregate score.<ref>{{Cite web |date=12 March 2024 |title=Barcelona 3-1 Napoli (4-2 on agg.): Robert Lewandowski among goals as Xavi's side make Champions League quarter-finals |url=https://www.tntsports.co.uk/football/champions-league/2023-2024/fc-barcelona-v-napoli-uefa-champions-league-live_sto10058242/story.shtml?welcome=eurosport |access-date=15 March 2024 |website=Eurosport |language=en |archive-date=24 August 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250824091728/https://www.tntsports.co.uk/football/champions-league/2023-2024/fc-barcelona-v-napoli-uefa-champions-league-live_sto10058242/story.shtml?welcome=eurosport |url-status=live }}</ref> On 17 March, he was a key player in Barcelona's 3–0 win over [[Atlético Madrid]] having been involved in all three goals. He scored one goal and produced two assists helping his side move to the second spot in the La Liga table.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.anews.com.tr/sport/2024/03/18/lewandowski-leads-barcelona-to-3-0-win-over-atletico-madrid |title=Lewandowski leads Barcelona to 3-0 win over Atletico Madrid |website=anews.com |date=18 March 2024 |access-date=18 March 2024 |archive-date=18 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240318073350/https://www.anews.com.tr/sport/2024/03/18/lewandowski-leads-barcelona-to-3-0-win-over-atletico-madrid |url-status=live }}</ref> On 29 April, he scored his first La Liga hat-trick to help his team get a 4–2 win against [[Valencia CF|Valencia]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.barcablaugranes.com/2024/4/29/24144557/barcelona-valencia-la-liga-final-score-match-report-recap-reactions |title=Barcelona vs Valencia, La Liga: Final Score 4-2, Robert Lewandowski scores decisive hat-trick as Barça complete hard-fought comeback at home |website=barcablaugranes.com |author=Renato Gonçalves |date=29 April 2024 |access-date=30 April 2024 |archive-date=29 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240429225453/https://www.barcablaugranes.com/2024/4/29/24144557/barcelona-valencia-la-liga-final-score-match-report-recap-reactions |url-status=live }}</ref>

====2024–25: Domestic double and 100 Barcelona goals====
On 17 August 2024, Lewandowski scored two goals in a 2–1 victory against [[Valencia CF|Valencia]]. It was the first match of the La Liga season for Barcelona and the first game with former Bayern Munich manager [[Hansi Flick]] in charge as the coach.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.eurosport.com/football/la-liga/2024-2025/valencia-v-barcelona-la-liga-live_sto10302703/story.shtml |title=Valencia 1-2 Barcelona - Robert Lewandowski scores twice as Barca come from behind to win in Hansi Flick's debut game |website=eurosport.com |author=Ciaran Baynes |access-date=18 August 2024 |archive-date=28 February 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250228065230/https://www.eurosport.com/football/la-liga/2024-2025/valencia-v-barcelona-la-liga-live_sto10302703/story.shtml |url-status=live }}</ref> On 22 September, Lewandowski scored two goals in a 5–1 victory against [[Villarreal CF|Villarreal]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.reuters.com/sports/soccer/lewandowski-raphinha-doubles-guide-barcelona-5-1-thrashing-villarreal-2024-09-22/ |title=Unstoppable Barcelona thrash Villarreal 5-1 with Lewandowski, Raphinha doubles |publisher=Reuters |access-date=23 September 2024}}</ref> On 25 September, he scored the winning goal in Barcelona's 1–0 victory over [[Getafe CF|Getafe]]. This was Lewandowski's 49th goal scored in La Liga beating [[Jan Urban]]'s record as the top scoring Polish player in La Liga history.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.eurosport.com/football/la-liga/2024-2025/barcelona-v-getafe-la-liga-live_sto10349465/story.shtml |title=La Liga: Robert Lewandowski strike earns Barcelona seventh straight league win to continue perfect start versus Getafe |website=eurosport.com |author=Ben Goddard |access-date=27 September 2024 |archive-date=25 September 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240925215243/https://www.eurosport.com/football/la-liga/2024-2025/barcelona-v-getafe-la-liga-live_sto10349465/story.shtml |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.goal.pl/la-liga/robert-lewandowski-jan-urban-barcelona-rekord/ |language=pl |title=Robert Lewandowski pobił rekord. Wyprzedził Jana Urbana |author=Ernest Chalimoniuk |website=goal.pl |date=25 September 2024 |access-date=27 September 2024 |archive-date=7 October 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241007100300/https://www.goal.pl/la-liga/robert-lewandowski-jan-urban-barcelona-rekord/ |url-status=live }}</ref> On 6 October, he scored a hat-trick in a 3–0 victory over [[Deportivo Alavés|Alavés]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/cvg37qre0zqt |title=Lewandowski hat-trick restores Barca lead at top of La Liga |publisher=BBC Sport |access-date=7 October 2024 |archive-date=8 October 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241008152542/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/cvg37qre0zqt |url-status=live }}</ref> On 20 October, Lewandowski scored two goals in a 5–1 victory against [[Sevilla FC|Sevilla]],<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5858173/2024/10/21/barcelona-lewandowski-gavi-flick-sevilla-cubarsi-la-liga/ |title=Barcelona 5 Sevilla 1: Lewandowski scores again, Gavi's emotional return, classy Cubarsi |website=[[The New York Times]] |author=Pol Ballús |date=21 October 2024 |access-date=21 October 2024 |archive-date=14 January 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250114182510/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5858173/2024/10/21/barcelona-lewandowski-gavi-flick-sevilla-cubarsi-la-liga/ |url-status=live }}</ref> in the process, he overtook [[Gerd Müller]]'s record and became the third highest scorer in the history of the five [[Big Five (association football)|major European football leagues]] with 366 goals in total.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.nogomania.com/read/Robert-Lewandowski-surpasses-Gerd-Muller-to-become-third-highest-scorer-in-Europe.aspx |title=Robert Lewandowski surpasses Gerd Müller to become third-highest scorer in Europe |website=nogomania.com |date=21 October 2024 |access-date=21 October 2024 |archive-date=7 December 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241207083416/https://www.nogomania.com/read/Robert-Lewandowski-surpasses-Gerd-Muller-to-become-third-highest-scorer-in-Europe.aspx |url-status=live }}</ref> 

On 23 October, Lewandowski scored the second goal in a 4–1 thrashing of his former club Bayern Munich in the Champions League, but did not celebrate out of respect for Bayern.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Kallas |first1=Fernando |date=23 October 2024 |title=Raphinha treble guides Barcelona to 4-1 rout of Bayern |url=https://www.reuters.com/sports/soccer/raphinha-treble-guides-barcelona-4-1-champions-league-thrashing-bayern-munich-2024-10-23/ |access-date=24 October 2024 |work=Reuters |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=23 October 2024 |title=Barcelona's Robert Lewandowski shows respect after netting vs Bayern Munich |url=https://ca.sports.yahoo.com/news/barcelona-robert-lewandowski-shows-respect-195100839.html |access-date=24 October 2024 |website=Yahoo Sports |language=en-CA |archive-date=7 December 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241207085420/https://ca.sports.yahoo.com/news/barcelona-robert-lewandowski-shows-respect-195100839.html |url-status=live }}</ref> Then on 26 October 2024, Lewandowski scored the first and second goal in Barcelona's 4–0 away demolition of [[Real Madrid CF|Real Madrid]] at the [[Santiago Bernabéu Stadium|Santiago Bernabéu]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=S.A |first=Telewizja Polska |title=Lewandowski's brace helps Barcelona thrash Real Madrid in European classic |url=https://tvpworld.com/83176240/el-clasico-lewandowskis-brace-helps-barcelona-thrash-real-madrid |access-date=27 October 2024 |website=tvpworld.com |language=pl |archive-date=5 November 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241105194254/https://tvpworld.com/83176240/el-clasico-lewandowskis-brace-helps-barcelona-thrash-real-madrid |url-status=live }}</ref> He was subsequently chosen [[La Liga Player of the Month]], his third such achievement.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.barcablaugranes.com/2024/11/1/24285412/barcelonas-robert-lewandowski-named-la-ligas-player-of-the-month-for-october |title=Barcelona's Robert Lewandowski named La Liga's Player of the Month for October |website=barcablaugranes.com |author=Gill Clark |date=1 November 2024 |access-date=2 November 2024 |archive-date=25 January 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250125045136/https://www.barcablaugranes.com/2024/11/1/24285412/barcelonas-robert-lewandowski-named-la-ligas-player-of-the-month-for-october |url-status=live }}</ref> On 23 November, he scored against [[RC Celta de Vigo|Celta Vigo]] in a match, which concluded in a 2–2 draw. By scoring this goal, Lewandowski recorded his 14th consecutive season in which he scored at least 20 goals for club, surpassing [[Lionel Messi]]'s record of 13.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.msn.com/pl-pl/sport/other/niezniszczalny-lewandowski-w%C5%82a%C5%9Bnie-przebi%C5%82-messiego/ar-AA1uEJ3w?ocid=msedgntp&pc=U531&cvid=9c5f84a780ff4ad39c449ddab947efa4&ei=6 |language=pl |title=Niezniszczalny. Lewandowski właśnie przebił Messiego |trans-title=Indestructible. Lewandowski just surpassed Messi |publisher=MSN |author=Damian Czykiel |date=24 November 2024 |access-date=24 November 2024 |archive-date=25 January 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250125045140/https://www.msn.com/pl-pl/sport/other/niezniszczalny-lewandowski-w%C5%82a%C5%9Bnie-przebi%C5%82-messiego/ar-AA1uEJ3w?ocid=msedgntp&pc=U531&cvid=9c5f84a780ff4ad39c449ddab947efa4&ei=6 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last= |date=2026-05-20 |title=How brilliant is Poland striker Robert Lewandowski? |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/0253-0d820e2c98c6-28c58e09e952-1000--how-brilliant-is-poland-striker-robert-lewandowski/ |access-date=2026-08-30 |publisher=[[UEFA]] |language=en |archive-date=30 August 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260830074408/https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/0253-0d820e2c98c6-28c58e09e952-1000--how-brilliant-is-poland-striker-robert-lewandowski/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Three days later, Lewandowski made history by netting a brace in Barcelona's 3–0 win over [[Stade Brestois 29|Brest]], his first goal in the match being his 100th Champions League goal. He became only the third player to pass the 100-goal mark in the Champions League.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/c4g718jl2l5o |title=How Lewandowski reached 100 Champions League goals |publisher=BBC Sport |date=26 November 2024 |access-date=27 November 2024 |archive-date=3 December 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241203145808/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/c4g718jl2l5o |url-status=live }}</ref> On 7 December, he netted a goal in a 2–2 draw against [[Real Betis]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.fcbarcelona.com/en/football/first-team/news/4182089/real-betis-2-2-fc-barcelona-late-despair |title=Real Betis 2-2 FC Barcelona: Late despair |publisher=FC Barcelona |author=Mike Roberts |date=7 December 2024 |access-date=10 December 2024 |archive-date=13 February 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250213184139/https://www.fcbarcelona.com/en/football/first-team/news/4182089/real-betis-2-2-fc-barcelona-late-despair |url-status=live }}</ref> By scoring the goal, Lewandowski reached 16 goals in his first 16 La Liga matches, equalling a record achieved by Messi during the [[2018–19 La Liga|2018–19 season]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.beinsports.com/en-us/soccer/la-liga/articles-video/robert-lewandowski-matches-lionel-messi-s-scoring-record-at-barcelona-2024-12-07 |title=Robert Lewandowski Matches Lionel Messi's Scoring Record at Barcelona |website=beinsports.com |access-date=10 December 2024 |archive-date=23 January 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250123041948/https://www.beinsports.com/en-us/soccer/la-liga/articles-video/robert-lewandowski-matches-lionel-messi-s-scoring-record-at-barcelona-2024-12-07 |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 9 April 2025, Lewandowski surpassed [[Cristiano Ronaldo]] as the player with the most goals past the age of thirty-five in the [[UEFA Champions League|Champions League]], 14.<ref>{{Cite web |last=UEFA.com |title=The official website for European football |url=https://www.uefa.com/errors/ |access-date=13 April 2025 |publisher=[[UEFA]] |language=en |archive-date=29 July 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200729205134/https://www.uefa.com/errors/ |url-status=live }}</ref> He reached this feat against former club [[Borussia Dortmund]] after scoring a brace in a 4–0 victory over the German side. Those goal involvements also led him to his 99th Barcelona goal, and becoming the [[Player of the match|Man of the Match]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/0298-1d7b80de9c63-9456d3c63fd3-1000--barcelona-4-0-borussia-dortmund-robert-lewandowski-hits-do/ |title=Barcelona 4-0 Borussia Dortmund: Robert Lewandowski hits double against former club in dominant win |publisher=UEFA |date=9 April 2025 |access-date=31 July 2025 |archive-date=24 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250724132538/https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/0298-1d7b80de9c63-9456d3c63fd3-1000--barcelona-4-0-borussia-dortmund-robert-lewandowski-hits-do/ |url-status=live }}</ref> He reached his 100th and 101st goals with the club in a 3–0 away win over [[Athletic Bilbao]] on the final matchday of the season.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20250525-lewandowski-passes-century-as-champions-barca-sign-off-in-style-at-athletic |title=Lewandowski passes century as champions Barca sign off in style at Athletic |publisher=France 24 |date=25 May 2025 |access-date=31 July 2025 |archive-date=27 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250527115922/https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20250525-lewandowski-passes-century-as-champions-barca-sign-off-in-style-at-athletic |url-status=live }}</ref> This made him join the small group of players to have scored 100 goals with three different clubs, and only the third player from the 21st century to do so after Cristiano Ronaldo and [[Neymar]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=6 August 2025 |title=Lewandowski joins CR7 and Neymar in post-2000 'Three-peat' club |url=https://onefootball.com/en/news/lewandowski-joins-cr7-and-neymar-in-post-2000-three-peat-club-41178172 |access-date=6 August 2025 |website=OneFootball |language=en |archive-date=24 August 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250824102446/https://onefootball.com/en/news/lewandowski-joins-cr7-and-neymar-in-post-2000-three-peat-club-41178172 |url-status=live }}</ref>

====2025–26: Third La Liga title and departure====
On 22 November 2025, the thirteenth matchday of the [[2025–26 La Liga|2025–26 La Liga]], Lewandowski scored the inaugural goal at the partially rebuilt [[Spotify]] [[Camp Nou]], having scored against Athletic Bilbao within four minutes in 4–0 victory.<ref>{{Cite web |date=22 November 2025 |title=Lewandowski will remember scoring first goal at new Camp Nou 'forever' |url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20251122-lewandowski-will-remember-scoring-first-goal-at-new-camp-nou-forever |access-date=22 November 2025 |publisher=France 24 |language=en |archive-date=22 November 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251122185143/https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20251122-lewandowski-will-remember-scoring-first-goal-at-new-camp-nou-forever |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=22 November 2025 |title=Barcelona return to Camp Nou with 4-0 win, 'a perfect day' |url=https://www.espn.co.uk/football/story/_/id/47059696/barcelona-return-camp-nou-4-0-win-perfect-day |access-date=22 November 2025 |publisher=[[ESPN]] |language=en |archive-date=22 November 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251122193138/https://www.espn.co.uk/football/story/_/id/47059696/barcelona-return-camp-nou-4-0-win-perfect-day |url-status=live }}</ref> In December 2025, he claimed Barcelona had previously asked him to avoid scoring by the end of the 2022–23 title-winning season in order to prevent triggering a bonus payment to his former club Bayern Munich.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.beinsports.com/en-us/soccer/la-liga/articles/lewandowski-claims-barcelona-asked-him-not-to-score-to-avoid-paying-bayern-bonus-2025-12-29 |title=Lewandowski claims Barcelona asked him not to score to avoid paying Bayern bonus |publisher=beIN SPORTS |date=29 December 2025 |access-date=30 December 2025 |archive-date=30 December 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251230044518/https://www.beinsports.com/en-us/soccer/la-liga/articles/lewandowski-claims-barcelona-asked-him-not-to-score-to-avoid-paying-bayern-bonus-2025-12-29 |url-status=live }}</ref> On 21 January 2026, he scored a goal in a 4–2 victory over [[SK Slavia Prague|Slavia Prague]], becoming only the fourth player to score in 15 consecutive seasons in the [[UEFA Champions League|Champions League]] after [[Lionel Messi]] and [[Karim Benzema]] with 18 each and [[Cristiano Ronaldo]] with 16.<ref>{{Cite news |last= |first= |date=21 January 2026 |title=Lewandowski scores for the 15th consecutive season in the Champions League |url=https://www.thestar.com/sports/soccer/lewandowski-scores-for-the-15th-consecutive-season-in-the-champions-league/article_774d5f08-a471-5c67-bdb7-fd52e2439d22.html |access-date=6 July 2026 |work=The Toronto Star |language=en-CA |issn=0319-0781 |archive-date=14 July 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260714031318/https://www.thestar.com/sports/soccer/lewandowski-scores-for-the-15th-consecutive-season-in-the-champions-league/article_774d5f08-a471-5c67-bdb7-fd52e2439d22.html |url-status=live }}</ref> On 7 February 2026, after scoring a goal in a 3–0 win against Mallorca, Lewandowski became the third player in the 21st century, after Ronaldo and Messi, to score at least 10 goals in [[Big Five (association football)|Europe's top five leagues]] for 15 consecutive seasons.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bonn |first=Kyle |date=7 February 2026 |title=Lewandowski equals goal record held only by Messi and Ronaldo as Barcelona extend La Liga lead |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/lewandowski-equals-goal-record-held-232348835.html |access-date=6 July 2026 |website=Yahoo Sports |language=en-US |archive-date=7 July 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260707161640/https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/lewandowski-equals-goal-record-held-232348835.html |url-status=live }}</ref> On 18 March 2026, Lewandowski scored a brace in a 7–2 victory over [[Newcastle United F.C.|Newcastle United]] during the [[2025–26 UEFA Champions League knockout phase|Champions League round of 16]], setting a new record by scoring against 41 different opponents in the tournament and surpassing the previous mark held by [[Lionel Messi]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.goal.com/en/lists/robert-lewandowski-breaks-lionel-messi-champions-league-record-double-newcastle-demolition/blt9db9c699cb1aa909 |title=Robert Lewandowski breaks Lionel Messi's Champions League record with double in Newcastle demolition |publisher=Goal.com |date=18 March 2026|last=Elgammal|first=Moataz}}</ref> He also became the oldest player to score in a Champions League knockout phase match at the age of 37 years and 209 days and the oldest player to score multiple goals in a Champions League match.<ref>{{Cite web |date=19 March 2026 |title=UCL Stats: Lewandowski breaks Messi's record with 41, Kane and Salah set milestones with 50 |url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/48245330/uefa-champions-league-ucl-stats-robert-lewandowski-breaks-lionel-messi-record-41-harry-kane-mohamed-salah-set-milestones-50 |access-date=6 July 2026 |publisher=[[ESPN]]}}</ref> A month later, on 25 April, he provided an assist in a 2–0 away win over Getafe, becoming the oldest player to reach 100 La Liga goal involvements (81 goals and 19 assists) in the 21st century, aged 37 years and 247 days.<ref>{{cite web |last=Anand |first=Anish |url=https://www.espn.co.uk/football/story/_/id/48606189/stats-robert-lewandowski-oldest-100-harry-kane-fastest-95 |title=Stats: Robert Lewandowski oldest to 100, Harry Kane fastest to 95 |publisher=ESPN |date=27 April 2026 |access-date=3 May 2026 |archive-date=28 April 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260428060902/https://www.espn.co.uk/football/story/_/id/48606189/stats-robert-lewandowski-oldest-100-harry-kane-fastest-95 |url-status=live }}</ref>

Lewandowski eventually won his third La Liga title with Barcelona, reaching a total of 14 league titles, including 13 in top five leagues, equaling the record of [[Ryan Giggs]], [[Thomas Müller]], [[Manuel Neuer]] and [[Kingsley Coman]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Żurek |first=Łukasz |url=https://sport.interia.pl/robert-lewandowski/news-lewandowski-na-to-tylko-czekal-to-juz-przesadzone-komunikat,nId,23475448 |title=Lewandowski na to tylko czekał. To już przesądzone. Komunikat tuż po gwizdku |publisher=Interia Sport |date=10 May 2026 |access-date=12 May 2026 |archive-date=12 May 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260512083949/https://sport.interia.pl/robert-lewandowski/news-lewandowski-na-to-tylko-czekal-to-juz-przesadzone-komunikat,nId,23475448 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Afroni |first=Donny |url=https://www.goal.com/en/lists/robert-lewandowski-admits-open-to-lower-league-transfer-amid-mls-links-barcelona-striker-issues-update-ahead-of-contract-expiry/bltd815c71ea9b8448f |title=Robert Lewandowski admits he's open to 'lower league' transfer amid MLS links as Barcelona striker issues update ahead of contract expiry |publisher=Goal.com |date=11 May 2026 |access-date=12 May 2026 |archive-date=12 May 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260512074644/https://www.goal.com/en/lists/robert-lewandowski-admits-open-to-lower-league-transfer-amid-mls-links-barcelona-striker-issues-update-ahead-of-contract-expiry/bltd815c71ea9b8448f |url-status=live }}</ref> On 16 May, he announced that he would depart the club at the end of the season.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.beinsports.com/en-mena/football/la-liga/articles-video/robert-lewandowski-announces-barcelona-exit-2026-05-16 |title=Robert Lewandowski announces Barcelona exit |publisher=beIN SPORTS |date=16 May 2026 |access-date=16 May 2026 |archive-date=6 June 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260606022926/https://www.beinsports.com/en-mena/football/la-liga/articles-video/robert-lewandowski-announces-barcelona-exit-2026-05-16 |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Chicago Fire===
On 29 June 2026, Lewandowski signed with [[Major League Soccer]] club [[Chicago Fire FC|Chicago Fire]], agreeing a contract running until 2028.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.chicagofirefc.com/news/a-defining-moment-in-chicago-sports-chicago-fire-fc-acquires-global-football-icon-robert-lewandowski |title=A Defining Moment in Chicago Sports: Chicago Fire FC Acquires Global Football Icon Robert Lewandowski |publisher=Chicago Fire FC |date=29 June 2026 |access-date=29 June 2026 |archive-date=29 June 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260629205420/https://www.chicagofirefc.com/news/a-defining-moment-in-chicago-sports-chicago-fire-fc-acquires-global-football-icon-robert-lewandowski |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.fox32chicago.com/sports/why-iconic-polish-striker-robert-lewandowski-chose-chicago-fire|title=Why iconic Polish striker Robert Lewandowski chose the Chicago Fire|first=Chris|last=Kwiecinski|date=July 14, 2026|publisher=FOX 32 Chicago|access-date=21 July 2026|archive-date=22 July 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260722023553/https://www.fox32chicago.com/sports/why-iconic-polish-striker-robert-lewandowski-chose-chicago-fire|url-status=live}}</ref> A month later, on 22 July, he made his debut in a 3–2 away defeat against [[Inter Miami CF|Inter Miami]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Kaufman |first=Michelle |url=https://www.miamiherald.com/sports/mls/inter-miami/article316595044.html |title=Inter Miami, without Messi, wins 3-2 as Lewandowski debuts for Chicago Fire |publisher=Miami Herald |date=22 July 2026 }}</ref> On 1 August, he scored his first goals, netting a brace in a 2–1 victory over [[Charlotte FC]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.espn.co.uk/football/report/_/gameId/761704 |title=Lewandowski nets brace in home debut as Chicago beats Charlotte |publisher=ESPN |date=2 August 2026 |access-date=2 August 2026 |archive-date=22 August 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260822014233/https://www.espn.co.uk/football/report/_/gameId/761704 |url-status=live }}</ref>

==International career==

===2007–2013: Youth level and early international career===
[[File:Robert Lewandowski 2011 (3).jpg|thumb|Lewandowski taking on [[József Varga (footballer, born 1988)|József Varga]] and [[Vilmos Vanczák]] of [[Hungary national football team|Hungary]] during a friendly match in 2011]]

Lewandowski began his international career with Poland [[Poland national under-19 football team|under-19]] in 2007.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Kumari |first=Payal |date=25 February 2022 |title=Everything You Need To Know About Robert Lewandowski: Debut, Teams, Goals, Records And Net Worth |url=https://sportsaxle.com/everything-you-need-to-know-about-robert-lewandowski-debut-teams-goals-records-and-net-worth/ |access-date=20 July 2022 |website=Sports Axle|archive-date=26 September 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220926100342/https://sportsaxle.com/everything-you-need-to-know-about-robert-lewandowski-debut-teams-goals-records-and-net-worth/ |url-status=live }}</ref> He would also make three appearances for [[Poland national under-21 football team|Poland's U21 team]], in friendly matches against [[England national under-21 football team|England]], [[Belarus national under-21 football team|Belarus]] and [[Finland national under-21 football team|Finland]].{{citation needed|date=July 2022}}

His debut for the senior national team came on 10 September 2008, three weeks after his 20th birthday, against [[San Marino national football team|San Marino]] where he came on as a substitute and scored a goal in a 2–0 away win in [[2010 FIFA World Cup qualification]].<ref>{{Cite news|first=Mudeet|last=Arora|title=How many goals has Robert Lewandowski scored for Poland? Barcelona star's full World Cup, Euro, Nations League and international friendly record|url=https://www.goal.com/en-sa/news/goals-robert-lewandowski-scored-poland-barcelona-world-cup-euro-nations-league-international-friendly-record/blt73a6f430e1d16955|website=[[Goal (website)|Goal]]|date=21 June 2023|access-date=10 June 2024|archive-date=10 June 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240610124638/https://www.goal.com/en-sa/news/goals-robert-lewandowski-scored-poland-barcelona-world-cup-euro-nations-league-international-friendly-record/blt73a6f430e1d16955|url-status=live}}</ref> Only [[Włodzimierz Lubański]] scored a goal on his debut for the national team at a younger age than Lewandowski, having been 16 at the time. Lewandowski scored another qualifying goal against the same team on 1 April 2009, in a 10–0 victory.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Mole |first=Giles |date=2 April 2009 |title=European World Cup qualifying round-up: Poland put 10 past woeful San Marino |work=The Daily Telegraph |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/football/world-cup/5093242/European-World-Cup-qualifying-round-up-Poland-put-10-past-woeful-San-Marino.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220110/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/football/world-cup/5093242/European-World-Cup-qualifying-round-up-Poland-put-10-past-woeful-San-Marino.html |archive-date=10 January 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |access-date=13 May 2015}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

Playing in Warsaw in the opening match of the [[UEFA Euro 2012]] tournament against [[Greece national football team|Greece]], Lewandowski scored the first goal of the competition after an assist from then Dortmund teammate [[Jakub Błaszczykowski]] and was named [[Man of the Match]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hart |first=Simon |date=8 June 2012 |title=Greece fightback foils Poland |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/history/news/0254-0d7dee5be59e-a226f3a4320b-1000--greece-fightback-foils-co-hosts-poland-in-euro-2012-group-a/ |access-date=1 December 2013 |publisher=UEFA |archive-date=10 February 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200210142541/https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/season%3D2012/matches/round%3D15172/match%3D2003319/postmatch/report/index.html |url-status=live }}</ref> He played in all three games for Poland in the tournament, as the co-hosts crashed out of the group stage with two points earned.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Holyman |first=Ian |date=16 June 2012 |title=Czechs through as Poland check out |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/history/news/0254-0d7e9fac6b78-bb120cc6ba96-1000--czech-republic-through-as-euro-2012-co-hosts-poland-chec/ |access-date=1 December 2013 |publisher=UEFA |archive-date=25 September 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170925180903/http://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/season=2012/matches/round=15172/match=2003336/postmatch/report/index.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=O'Henley |first=Alex |date=17 June 2012 |title=Over and out for Poland |url=http://www.uefa.com/news/newsid=1804253.html |access-date=1 December 2013 |publisher=UEFA |archive-date=3 December 2013 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131203011857/http://www.uefa.com/news/newsid=1804253.html |url-status=dead }}</ref>

===2013–2017: Assuming captaincy===
[[File:Lewandowski and Milik vs Ireland 2013.jpg|thumb|right|Lewandowski playing for [[Poland national football team|Poland]] against [[Republic of Ireland national football team|Ireland]] in 2013]]
Lewandowski scored two penalties in the 5–0 win against San Marino on 26 March 2013 during the [[2014 FIFA World Cup qualification (UEFA)|2014 World Cup qualifying campaign]], his first match as [[Captain (association football)|captain]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=26 March 2013 |title=Lewandowski-inspired Poland beat San Marino |publisher=UEFA |url=http://www.uefa.com/worldcup/season=2014/matches/round=2000294/match=2008742/postmatch/report/index.html |access-date=13 May 2015 |archive-date=25 September 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170925181341/http://www.uefa.com/worldcup/season=2014/matches/round=2000294/match=2008742/postmatch/report/index.html |url-status=dead }}</ref> Later on in the campaign, on 6 September, he scored the equaliser against [[Montenegro national football team|Montenegro]] in a 1–1 home draw.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Olkowicz |first1=Łukasz |last2=Żelazny |first2=Piotr |date=6 September 2013 |title=Polska – Czarnogóra 1:1. Futbol po raz kolejny okazał się okrutny |trans-title=Poland – Montenegro 1:1. Football has once again proved to be cruel |url=http://pilka-nozna.przegladsportowy.pl/Pilka-nozna-Polska-Czarnogora-1-1-w-eliminacjach-Ms-2014,artykul,180555,1,291.html |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130927132434/http://pilka-nozna.przegladsportowy.pl/Pilka-nozna-Polska-Czarnogora-1-1-w-eliminacjach-Ms-2014,artykul,180555,1,291.html |archive-date=27 September 2013 |access-date=1 December 2013 |website=[[Przegląd Sportowy]] |language=pl}}</ref> Poland did not qualify for the [[2014 FIFA World Cup|2014 World Cup]] in Brazil.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Grant |first=Ethan |title=England Qualify for 2014 World Cup with 2-0 Win over Poland |url=https://bleacherreport.com/articles/1812595-england-qualify-for-2014-world-cup-with-2-0-win-over-poland |access-date=20 July 2022 |website=Bleacher Report |language=en |archive-date=20 July 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220720021717/https://bleacherreport.com/articles/1812595-england-qualify-for-2014-world-cup-with-2-0-win-over-poland |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 7 September 2014, in Poland's first [[UEFA Euro 2016 qualifying|UEFA Euro 2016 qualifier]], away against [[Gibraltar national football team|Gibraltar]], Lewandowski scored his first international hat-trick, netting four goals in a 7–0 win.<ref>{{Cite news |date=7 September 2014 |title=Poland's Robert Lewandowski scores four in seven-goal rout of Gibraltar |work=[[The Guardian]] |agency=[[Press Association]] |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/sep/07/poland-gibraltar-euro-2016--match-report |access-date=11 October 2014 |archive-date=1 October 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181001053829/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/sep/07/poland-gibraltar-euro-2016--match-report |url-status=live }}</ref> On 13 June 2015, he scored another hat-trick in Poland's 4–0 defeat of [[Georgia national football team|Georgia]], with the three goals scored within the space of four minutes.<ref>{{Cite news |date=13 June 2015 |title=Drei Tore von Lewandowski bei Polens 4:0 |work=Neue Zürcher Zeitung |url=http://www.nzz.ch/sport/drei-tore-von-lewandowski-bei-polens-40-1.18561613 |language=de |access-date=13 June 2015 |archive-date=26 February 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200226002743/http://www.nzz.ch/sport/drei-tore-von-lewandowski-bei-polens-40-1.18561613 |url-status=live }}</ref> On 8 October, he scored twice in a 2–2 draw away to [[Scotland national football team|Scotland]], opening and equalising with the last kick of the game to eliminate the hosts.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lamont |first=Alasdair |date=8 October 2015 |title=Scotland 2–2 Poland |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/33543822 |access-date=12 October 2015 |publisher=BBC Sport |archive-date=21 January 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160121212248/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/33543822 |url-status=live }}</ref> Three days later he headed the winner in a 2–1 victory against the [[Republic of Ireland national football team|Republic of Ireland]], qualifying Poland for the tournament finals in France.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Koźmiński |first=Piotr |date=11 October 2015 |title=Lewandowski's latest takes Poland to France |url=https://www.uefa.com/european-qualifiers/news/0253-0d805627bf50-4b0fa69e6b10-1000--lewandowski-s-latest-takes-poland-to-france/ |access-date=15 October 2015 |publisher=UEFA |archive-date=15 October 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151015003007/http://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/qualifiers/season=2016/matches/round=2000446/match=2014050/postmatch/report/index.html |url-status=live }}</ref> Lewandowski ended the campaign with 13 goals, a joint [[UEFA European Championship qualifying|European Championships qualifying]] record with [[David Healy (footballer)|David Healy]]'s tally for [[Northern Ireland national football team|Northern Ireland]] in [[UEFA Euro 2008 qualifying]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=12 October 2015 |title=Lewandowski equals Healy's scoring record |url=https://www.uefa.com/european-qualifiers/news/0253-0d80578af302-67dcd0042fc2-1000--lukaku-sets-new-european-qualifiers-scoring-record/ |access-date=12 October 2015 |publisher=UEFA |archive-date=14 November 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151114015938/http://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/qualifiers/news/newsid=2292506.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

At [[UEFA Euro 2016]] in France, Lewandowski did not have a shot on target until the last-16 match against [[Switzerland national football team|Switzerland]] in [[Saint-Étienne]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Brassell |first=Andy |date=25 June 2016 |title=Poland hold nerve after Switzerland's Granit Xhaka blazes penalty wide |work=The Guardian |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2016/jun/25/switzerland-poland-euro-2016-match-report |access-date=30 June 2016 |archive-date=1 August 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200801041625/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2016/jun/25/switzerland-poland-euro-2016-match-report |url-status=live }}</ref> Following the 1–1 draw, he scored his team's first attempt in the penalty shootout victory that sent them to the quarter-finals for the first time.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Johnston |first=Neil |date=25 June 2016 |title=Switzerland 1–1 Poland |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/36566078 |access-date=30 June 2016 |publisher=BBC Sport |archive-date=28 June 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160628160837/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/36566078 |url-status=live }}</ref> In the 100th second of the quarter-final against [[Portugal national football team|Portugal]] at the [[Stade Vélodrome]], he finished [[Kamil Grosicki]]'s cross to open another 1–1 draw, and again scored in the shootout although the Poles lost.<ref name="portugal">{{Cite web |last=Dawkes |first=Phil |date=30 June 2016 |title=Poland 1–1 Portugal |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/36603665 |access-date=30 June 2016 |publisher=BBC Sport |archive-date=22 May 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210522120130/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/36603665 |url-status=live }}</ref> At the time of Poland's exit, Lewandowski had suffered more fouls than any other player in the tournament.<ref name=portugal/>

===2017–2026: All-time Poland top scorer, short-lived retirement===
[[File:Robert Lewandowski 2018, JAP-POL (cropped).jpg|thumb|upright|Lewandowski playing for [[Poland national football team|Poland]] at the [[2018 FIFA World Cup]]]]
On 5 October 2017, Lewandowski scored a hat-trick in a 6–1 victory against [[Armenia national football team|Armenia]] to take his tally to 50 goals for Poland, surpassing the previous record of 48 goals set by [[Włodzimierz Lubański]] to become the all-time top scorer for Poland.<ref>{{Cite news |date=5 October 2017 |title=Robert Lewandowski becomes Poland's all-time leading scorer |publisher=ESPN|url=http://www.espnfc.com/poland/story/3221099/robert-lewandowski-becomes-polands-all-time-leading-scorer |access-date=5 October 2017 |archive-date=30 December 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191230051537/http://www.espnfc.com/poland/story/3221099/robert-lewandowski-becomes-polands-all-time-leading-scorer |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Lewandowski breaks Ronaldo's European Qualifiers goal record |url=https://www.uefa.com/european-qualifiers/news/newsid=2497563.html |access-date=5 October 2017 |archive-date=21 October 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171021012534/http://www.uefa.com/european-qualifiers/news/newsid=2497563.html |url-status=dead }}</ref> On 8 October, Lewandowski scored a goal in a 4–2 victory against Montenegro, taking his tally to 51 goals for Poland.<ref name="Bundesliga">{{Cite news |date=10 October 2017 |title=Bayern Munich's Robert Lewandowski sets European scoring record for Poland|publisher=Bundesliga |url=http://www.bundesliga.com/en/news/Bundesliga/robert-lewandowski-sets-world-cup-qualifying-goal-record-ahead-of-ronaldo-461228.jsp |access-date=10 October 2017 |archive-date=28 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210128050128/https://www.bundesliga.com/en/news/Bundesliga/robert-lewandowski-sets-world-cup-qualifying-goal-record-ahead-of-ronaldo-461228.jsp |url-status=live }}</ref> He finished the [[2018 FIFA World Cup qualification]] campaign with a total of 16 goals, a record for a European World Cup qualification.<ref name="Bundesliga" />

Lewandowski was called up to the [[2018 FIFA World Cup squads#Poland|23-man Polish squad]] for the [[2018 FIFA World Cup]] in Russia.<ref>{{Cite news|title=Poland World Cup squad guide: Full fixtures, group, ones to watch, odds |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/world-cup/poland-world-cup-squad-profile-russia-2018-fixtures-group-team-news-schedule-a8393021.html |access-date=8 July 2018 |newspaper=The Independent |archive-date=9 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180709043721/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/world-cup/poland-world-cup-squad-profile-russia-2018-fixtures-group-team-news-schedule-a8393021.html |url-status=live }}</ref> Lewandowski played every minute in all three matches against [[Senegal national football team|Senegal]], [[Colombia national football team|Colombia]], and [[Japan national football team|Japan]]. He did not score any goals and Poland failed to qualify for the knockout phase.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Poland |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/teams/team=43962/index.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20071129220613/http://www.fifa.com/worldcup/teams/team=43962/index.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=29 November 2007 |access-date=8 July 2018 |publisher=FIFA}}</ref>

On 19 June 2021, in Poland's second group stage match of [[UEFA Euro 2020]] against [[Spain national football team|Spain]], Lewandowski scored the equalising goal in a 1–1 draw. He became the first Polish player to score in three consecutive [[UEFA European Championship|European Championships]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/51197624 |title=Lewandowski scores as Poland hold Spain|publisher=BBC Sport |date=19 June 2021 |access-date=19 June 2021 |archive-date=19 June 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210619113417/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/51197624 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.squawka.com/en/euro-2020-group-e-second-round-spain-poland-sweden-slovakia/ |title=Poland duo make history against Spain to take Euro 2020 Group E to an exciting final day|website=Squawka|date=19 June 2021 |access-date=19 June 2021 |archive-date=28 June 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210628175749/https://www.squawka.com/en/euro-2020-group-e-second-round-spain-poland-morata-lewandowski/ |url-status=live }}</ref> On 23 June, he scored a brace in a 3–2 defeat against [[Sweden men's national football team|Sweden]], but Poland finished last in their group and were knocked out in the group stage.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.euronews.com/2021/06/23/lewandowski-poland-out-of-euro-2020-with-3-2-loss-to-sweden |title=Lewandowski, Poland out of Euro 2020 with 3–2 loss to Sweden |website=EuroNews|date=23 June 2021 |access-date=23 June 2021 |archive-date=23 June 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210623195357/https://www.euronews.com/2021/06/23/lewandowski-poland-out-of-euro-2020-with-3-2-loss-to-sweden |url-status=live }}</ref>

Lewandowski was selected for the [[2022 FIFA World Cup squads#Poland|national squad]] ahead of the [[2022 FIFA World Cup]] in Qatar. During the first match against [[Mexico national football team|Mexico]], he missed a penalty in an eventual scoreless draw.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Lewandowski misses penalty as Mexico hold Poland|publisher=BBC Sport |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/63631782 |access-date=23 November 2022 |archive-date=22 November 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221122221148/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/63631782 |url-status=live }}</ref> However, in the second match against [[Saudi Arabia national football team|Saudi Arabia]], Lewandowski scored his first [[FIFA World Cup]] goal in a 2–0 Poland win.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Howarth |first=Matt |date=26 November 2022 |title=Lewandowski scores first World Cup goal in Poland win|publisher=BBC Sport|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/63685897 |access-date=26 November 2022 |archive-date=25 November 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221125224623/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/63685897 |url-status=live }}</ref> He scored his second World Cup goal on a penalty in a 3–1 loss against [[France national football team|France]] in the round of 16.<ref>{{cite news |title=Giroud and Mbappé fire France into quarter-finals |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/63771032 |access-date=4 December 2022 |publisher=BBC Sport |archive-date=3 January 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230103080251/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/63771032 |url-status=live }}</ref>

In June 2024, Lewandowski was named in the final 26-man [[UEFA Euro 2024 squads#Poland|squad]] for [[UEFA Euro 2024]] in Germany.<ref>{{cite web|title=Michał Probierz ogłosił kadrę na Euro 2024 |url=https://pzpn.pl/reprezentacje/reprezentacja-a/aktualnosci/2024-06-07/michal-probierz-oglosil-kadre-na-euro-2024 |publisher=[[Polish Football Association]] |access-date=7 June 2024 |language=pl |date=7 June 2024}}</ref> In Poland's third group stage game, he converted a penalty kick to equalize in a 1–1 draw against France, but Poland exited the tournament after finishing at the bottom of their group.<ref>{{cite web |first=Wojciech |last=Papuga |title=Remis z Francją. Reprezentacja Polski zatrzymała wicemistrzów świata! [Wideo]|url=https://sport.tvp.pl/78853384/remis-z-francja-reprezentacja-polski-zatrzymala-wicemistrzow-swiata |website=TVP Sport|access-date=25 June 2024 |language=pl |date=25 June 2024}}</ref>

Lewandowski was not called up for two June 2025 matches against [[Moldova national football team|Moldova]] and [[Finland national football team|Finland]], citing exhaustion after the end of the club season.<ref>{{cite web |last=Kłyszejko|first=Jakub |title=Robert Lewandowski nie zagra w czerwcowych meczach reprezentacji Polski z Mołdawią i Finlandią! |url=https://sport.tvp.pl/86918079/robert-lewandowski-nie-zagra-w-czerwcowych-meczach-reprezentacji-polski-z-moldawia-i-finlandia |website=TVP Sport|access-date=8 June 2025 |language=pl |date=26 May 2025}}</ref> On 8 June, following the decision of head coach [[Michał Probierz]] to name [[Piotr Zieliński]] new captain of the Poland national team, Lewandowski announced he would not play for the national team as long as Probierz was the manager. Following Lewandowski's remarks and Poland's defeat against Finland in the 2026 World Cup qualifiers, Probierz resigned.<ref>{{cite web |last=Wieczorek |first=Bartosz |title=Robert Lewandowski zrezygnował z gry w reprezentacji Polski! Podał powód |url=https://sport.tvp.pl/87169259/robert-lewandowski-zrezygnowal-z-gry-w-reprezentacji-polski-podal-powod |website=TVP Sport|access-date=8 June 2025 |language=pl |date=8 June 2025}}</ref>

Following the appointment of [[Jan Urban]] as Poland manager on 16 July 2025,<ref>{{Cite web |last=S.A |first=Telewizja Polska |title=Veteran Jan Urban appointed new Poland manager |url=https://tvpworld.com/87868862/veteran-jan-urban-appointed-new-poland-football-manager |access-date=4 August 2025 |website=tvpworld.com |language=pl}}</ref> reports of Lewandowski's national team return ahead of the September matches against the Netherlands and Finland surfaced.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bhawani |first=Vishal |date=18 July 2025 |title=Robert Lewandowski makes national team call after new head coach appointment |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/article/robert-lewandowski-makes-national-team-120806564.html |access-date=4 August 2025 |website=Yahoo Sports |language=en-US}}</ref> In August 2025, he was selected for the September games and reinstated as Poland's captain.<ref>{{cite web |title=Robert Lewandowski ponownie kapitanem reprezentacji Polski. Selekcjoner Jan Urban przekazał decyzję |url=https://eurosport.tvn24.pl/pilka-nozna/eliminacje-ms-europa/2026/robert-lewandowski-ponownie-kapitanem-reprezentacji-polski.-selekcjoner-jan-urban-przekazal-decyzje_sto23216013/story.shtml |website=eurosport.tvn24.pl |access-date=29 August 2025 |language=pl |date=29 August 2025 |trans-title=Robert Lewandowski is once again the captain of the Polish national team. Coach Jan Urban announced the decision}}</ref>

After a 3–2 away loss against [[Sweden men's national football team|Sweden]] in the [[2026 FIFA World Cup qualification – UEFA second round|2026 World Cup play-offs final]] on 31 March 2026, Lewandowski strongly hinted at retiring from international football following Poland's failure to qualify for the [[2026 FIFA World Cup|2026 World Cup]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=1 April 2026 |title=Robert Lewandowski hints at international retirement after Poland misses out on World Cup |url=https://apnews.com/article/robert-lewandowski-poland-retirement-20aad1e1aea7ad82d12367fee74657cf |access-date=1 April 2026 |publisher=Associated Press |language=en}}</ref> Nevertheless, Lewandowski featured in Poland's friendly matches against [[Ukraine national football team|Ukraine]] and [[Nigeria national football team|Nigeria]] two months later, losing the former, drawing the latter, and scoring in neither.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.espn.co.uk/espn/story/_/id/48963021/nigeria-show-depth-late-lapse-costs-victory-lewandowsi-poland |access-date=10 June 2026 |publisher=[[ESPN]]|title=Nigeria show depth but late lapse costs victory over Lewandowsi's Poland|date=4 June 2026|last=Udoh|first=Colin}}</ref>

==Style of play==
[[File:20190428 DFL 1. Bundesliga FCN - FCB 850 0565.jpg|left|thumb|Lewandowski playing against [[1. FC Nürnberg]] in 2019]]
Lewandowski was widely regarded as one of the best strikers of all-time,<ref>{{Cite news |date=22 October 2019 |title=Robert Lewandowski: Is the Bayern Munich player the world's best striker right now? |work=BBC Sport |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/50145108 |access-date=20 August 2020 |archive-date=24 October 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191024235246/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/50145108 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Gheerbrant |first=James |title=Robert Lewandowski – the planet's best striker – deserves European glory with Bayern Munich |work=[[The Times]] |date=1 June 2020 |url=https://www.thetimes.com/sport/football/article/robert-lewandowski-the-planet-s-best-striker-deserves-european-glory-with-bayern-munich-7bqrhtxlw |access-date=20 August 2020 |url-access=subscription |archive-date=21 October 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201021125751/https://www.thetimes.co.uk/article/robert-lewandowski-the-planet-s-best-striker-deserves-european-glory-with-bayern-munich-7bqrhtxlw |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Bayern Munich's Robert Lewandowski the world's best striker? |url=https://www.bundesliga.com/en/news/Bundesliga/bayern-munich-s-robert-lewandowski-world-s-best-striker-456853.jsp |access-date=20 August 2020 |website=bundesliga.com |archive-date=22 September 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200922153912/https://www.bundesliga.com/en/news/Bundesliga/bayern-munich-s-robert-lewandowski-world-s-best-striker-456853.jsp |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=27 November 2019 |title=Ranked! The 10 best strikers in the world |url=https://www.fourfourtwo.com/features/best-strikers-in-the-world-ronaldo-lewandowski-harry-kane |access-date=20 August 2020 |work=FourFourTwo |archive-date=26 December 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201226115439/https://www.fourfourtwo.com/features/best-strikers-in-the-world-ronaldo-lewandowski-harry-kane |url-status=live }}</ref> and is considered by many to be one of the greatest centre-forwards ever.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hepburn |first=Daniel |date=10 July 2025 |title=Thierry Henry had no doubt when naming the 'greatest striker of this generation' - not Ronaldo |url=https://www.givemesport.com/thierry-henry-named-greatest-striker-this-generation/ |access-date=23 July 2025 |website=GiveMeSport |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=31 January 2025 |title=Is Harry Kane the best No.9 of his generation? Bayern Munich star ranked against Robert Lewandowski, Luis Suarez & Sergio Aguero as England captain is backed to emulate Lionel Messi & Cristiano Ronaldo &#124; Goal.com UK |url=https://www.goal.com/en-gb/lists/harry-kane-best-no-9-generation-bayern-munich-robert-lewandowski-luis-suarez-sergio-aguero-england-emulate-lionel-messi-cristiano-ronaldo/bltfbcefdb11f4d3752 |access-date=23 July 2025 |website=goal.com |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Panja |first=Tariq |date=13 September 2024 |title=Robert Lewandowski on Fame, Frailty and the One Voice He Won't Ignore |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/09/13/world/europe/robert-lewandowski-barcelona.html |access-date=23 July 2025 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> An accurate and efficient finisher with his head and both feet, Lewandowski is a prolific goalscorer, which has led him to be dubbed ''Lewangoalski''.<ref>{{Cite web |title=LewanGOALski Nickname - What does it mean and how did it come about? - Player Biography and Profile |url=https://www.sports-king.com/nicknames.php?q=lewangoalski |access-date=30 May 2022 |website=sports-king.com |archive-date=30 May 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220530153210/https://www.sports-king.com/nicknames.php?q=lewangoalski |url-status=live }}</ref> A well-rounded [[Forward (association football)|forward]], he is said to possess almost all the necessary qualities of a traditional [[Squad number (association football)|number nine]]: height, strength, balance, pace, intelligent movement and proficiency with both feet.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Haugstad |first=Thore |date=10 October 2015 |title=How Robert Lewandowski became this season's deadliest striker |url=http://www.espnfc.co.uk/blog/tactics-and-analysis/67/post/2653540/how-robert-lewandowski-became-this-seasons-deadliest-striker |access-date=16 July 2016 |publisher=[[ESPN FC]] |archive-date=13 August 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160813004736/http://www.espnfc.co.uk/blog/tactics-and-analysis/67/post/2653540/how-robert-lewandowski-became-this-seasons-deadliest-striker |url-status=live }}</ref> Although he primarily operates as a goal-poacher in the penalty area, due to his positional sense, ability to shoot first time, strength in the air, and powerful shot with either foot, his excellent technical skills, quick feet, proficient [[Dribbling#Association football|dribbling]], vision, and physique also enable him to hold up the ball with his back to goal and either bring his teammates into play, or win fouls for his team in useful positions. Despite often functioning as a lone-[[centre forward]] or as an out-and-out [[Striker (association football)|striker]], he has also stood out for his work-rate and defensive contribution off the ball, and is capable of dropping into deeper roles on the pitch, in order to create space for teammates with his movement, or surprise defenders by making late and sudden attacking runs into the area. He became more of a team player as his career progressed, having been criticised by pundits earlier in his career for his perceived selfishness.

Lewandowski is an accurate [[Penalty kick (association football)|penalty]] taker and has repeatedly shown coolness and composure on the spot; he is also capable of scoring from long range, and has been known to take [[Free kick (association football)|free kicks]]. In addition to his playing ability, Lewandowski has also been praised for his outstanding work-ethic, fitness, mentality, and discipline, both on the pitch and in training, by pundits, players and managers;<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bull |first=JJ |date=20 October 2015 |title=Robert Lewandowski: how he became the most prolific striker in Europe |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/football/teams/bayern-munich/11928742/Robert-Lewandowski-how-he-became-the-most-prolific-striker-in-Europe.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220110/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/football/teams/bayern-munich/11928742/Robert-Lewandowski-how-he-became-the-most-prolific-striker-in-Europe.html |archive-date=10 January 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |access-date=19 December 2016 |website=The Telegraph}}{{cbignore}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last1=Koźmiński |last2=Röber |first2=Philip |date=17 November 2016 |title=How brilliant is Bayern's Robert Lewandowski? |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/0253-0d820e2c98c6-28c58e09e952-1000--how-brilliant-is-barcelona-and-poland-striker-robert-lewand/ |access-date=19 December 2016 |publisher=UEFA |archive-date=16 January 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200116034658/https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/newsid=2422428.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="Fortitude">{{Cite web |last=Christenson |first=Marcus |date=24 May 2013 |title=Robert Lewandowski brings goals and fortitude to Borussia Dortmund |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/blog/2013/may/24/robert-lewandowski-goals-borussia-dortmund |access-date=19 December 2016 |website=The Guardian |archive-date=7 August 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200807030506/https://www.theguardian.com/football/blog/2013/may/24/robert-lewandowski-goals-borussia-dortmund |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Rapp |first=Timothy |date=4 January 2014 |title=Robert Lewandowski to Bayern Munich: FC Bayern Sign Polish Striker |url=https://bleacherreport.com/articles/1653304-robert-lewandowski-to-bayern-munich-fc-bayern-reportedly-sign-polish-striker |access-date=25 April 2021 |publisher=Bleacher Report |archive-date=25 April 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210425193041/https://bleacherreport.com/articles/1653304-robert-lewandowski-to-bayern-munich-fc-bayern-reportedly-sign-polish-striker |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Philippe Coutinho, Robert Lewandowski and David Alaba: Do Bayern Munich have the best free-kick takers? |url=https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/philippe-coutinho-lewandowski-alaba-bayern-munich-best-free-kick-takers-7654 |access-date=25 April 2021 |publisher=bundesliga.com |archive-date=25 April 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210425193040/https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/philippe-coutinho-lewandowski-alaba-bayern-munich-best-free-kick-takers-7654 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news|first=Raphael|last=Honigstein|url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/1321197/2019/10/28/lewandowski/ |title=From 'more selfish than Robben' to staying late to teach young strikers: how and why Lewandowski has changed |work=The Athletic|date=28 October 2019 |access-date=1 May 2024 }}</ref> his disciplined approach to training and fitness has led to him being nicknamed "The Body".<ref>{{Cite news |last=AFP |date=17 December 2020 |title=Robert Lewandowski, 'The Body' Who Put Messi And Ronaldo In Shade |url=https://www.barrons.com/news/robert-lewandowski-the-body-who-put-messi-and-ronaldo-in-shade-01608239109 |access-date=15 January 2025 |work=[[Barron's]]}}</ref>

==Outside football==

===Personal life===
[[File:Robert Lewandowski 2010 (1).jpg|thumb|upright|right|Lewandowski in 2010]]
Lewandowski's father gave him the name Robert to make it easier for him when moving abroad as a professional footballer.<ref name="Fortitude"/> Lewandowski's father, Krzysztof (died in 2005),<ref>{{Cite web |last=Michalak |first=Przemysław |date=16 June 2013 |title=Lewandowski: Ojciec zmarł w 2005 roku. Wszystkie gole dedykuję jemu |url=http://www.2x45.info/aktualnosci/17751/lewandowski-ojciec-zmarl-w-2005-roku-wszystkie-gole-dedykuje-jemu/ |publisher=2x45 Info |access-date=10 April 2019 |archive-date=30 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231030215157/http://www.2x45.info/aktualnosci/17751/lewandowski-ojciec-zmarl-w-2005-roku-wszystkie-gole-dedykuje-jemu/ |url-status=live }}</ref> was a Polish [[judo]] champion, and also played football for [[Hutnik Warsaw]] in the second division.{{citation needed|date=April 2026}} His mother, Iwona, is a former [[volleyball]] player for [[AZS Politechnika Warsaw|AZS Warsaw]] and later vice-president of Partyzant Leszno.{{citation needed|date=April 2026}} His sister, Milena, also plays volleyball and has represented the U21 national team.{{citation needed|date=April 2026}}

His wife, [[Anna Lewandowska]] (née Stachurska), won the bronze medal at the 2009 [[Karate]] World Cup.{{citation needed|date=April 2026}} They married on 22 June 2013 in the [[Serock#Church of the Annunciation of the Blessed Virgin Mary|Church of the Annunciation of the Blessed Virgin Mary]] in [[Serock]]. They have two children, born in 2017 and 2020<!--Please see [[WP:BLPNAME]].-->.<ref>{{Cite web |date=4 May 2017 |title=Stolzer Papa von Klara |trans-title=Proud Dad of Klara |url=http://www.spiegel.de/panorama/leute/fc-bayern-muenchen-robert-lewandowski-ist-vater-geworden-a-1146126.html |access-date=4 May 2017 |website=Der Spiegel |language=de |archive-date=19 March 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180319095414/http://www.spiegel.de/panorama/leute/fc-bayern-muenchen-robert-lewandowski-ist-vater-geworden-a-1146126.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=6 May 2020 |title=Robert Lewandowski: Second daughter born – 'Welcome to the world, Laura' |url=https://www.en24.news/en/2020/05/robert-lewandowski-second-daughter-born-welcome-to-the-world-laurahtml |access-date=6 May 2020 |website=En24 News }}{{Dead link|date=July 2023 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref>

Lewandowski is a practising [[Catholic Church in Poland|Catholic]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=12 June 2018 |title=Famous football player Robert Lewandowski is not ashamed of Jesus. Video in 8 languages |work=Polonia Christiana |publisher=Father Piotr Skarga Association for Christian Culture |location=Kraków |url=https://www.eng.pch24.pl/famous-football-player-robert-lewandowski-is-not-ashamed-of-jesus--video-in-8-languages-,60911,i.html |access-date=10 April 2019 |archive-date=6 August 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200806194016/https://www.eng.pch24.pl/famous-football-player-robert-lewandowski-is-not-ashamed-of-jesus--video-in-8-languages-,60911,i.html |url-status=dead }}</ref> He met [[Pope Francis]] in October 2014, when Bayern Munich visited [[Vatican City]] following a 7–1 win over [[A.S. Roma|Roma]] in the [[2014–15 UEFA Champions League group stage#Group E|UEFA Champions League]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=22 October 2014 |title=Bayern Munich: Pope praises German club after win over Roma |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/29729737 |access-date=24 October 2014 |publisher=BBC Sport |archive-date=18 December 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201218124158/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/29729737 |url-status=live }}</ref>

In October 2017, the day after scoring to help Poland qualify for the 2018 World Cup, Lewandowski finished his [[Bachelor of Physical Education]] (BPhEd) with coaching and management at the Academy of Sport Education in Warsaw, concluding a decade of studies.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Burton |first=Chris |date=10 October 2017 |title=Bayern striker Lewandowski gets a degree... after writing about himself |work=Goal |publisher=Perform Group |location=Leeds |url=https://www.goal.com/en/news/bayern-striker-lewandowski-gets-a-bachelors-degree-after-writing-/jl5t25q4k2bk10hcjfkh6r0fc |access-date=5 June 2019 |archive-date=18 August 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200818102910/https://www.goal.com/en/news/bayern-striker-lewandowski-gets-a-bachelors-degree-after-writing-/jl5t25q4k2bk10hcjfkh6r0fc |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=10 October 2017 |title=School's out for Robert Lewandowski as Bayern Munich striker completes decade-long university studies |publisher=Bundesliga |location=Frankfurt |url=https://www.bundesliga.com/en/news/Bundesliga/bayern-munich-s-robert-lewandowski-completes-university-course-461260.jsp |access-date=7 September 2018 |archive-date=23 May 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210523203812/https://www.bundesliga.com/en/news/Bundesliga/bayern-munich-s-robert-lewandowski-completes-university-course-461260.jsp |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=8 October 2017 |title=Lewandowski: Wczoraj awansował do mundialu, dziś obronił pracę licencjacką |url=https://www.przegladsportowy.pl/pilka-nozna/reprezentacja-polski/lewandowski-dzis-awans-jutro-licencjat/1ph2exn |website=Przegląd Sportowy |access-date=13 June 2020 |archive-date=10 June 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200610111804/https://www.przegladsportowy.pl/pilka-nozna/reprezentacja-polski/lewandowski-dzis-awans-jutro-licencjat/1ph2exn |url-status=live }}</ref>

In addition to his native [[Polish language|Polish]], Lewandowski also speaks English and German.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Leadership League: Robert Lewandowski &#124; Leadership League |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Eep--Dny8oc |access-date=19 July 2020 |website=CNBC International TV |via=YouTube |archive-date=2 May 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210502011854/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Eep--Dny8oc |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=FC Bayern Press Conference w/ Robert Lewandowski &#124; ReLive |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Sp_Yk5d8I1Y |access-date=19 July 2020 |publisher=FC Bayern Munich |via=YouTube |archive-date=19 December 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201219191718/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Sp_Yk5d8I1Y |url-status=live }}</ref>

Lewandowski is a fan of [[tennis]] and [[paddle tennis]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://przegladsportowy.onet.pl/ofsajd/robert-lewandowski-pokazal-jak-gra-w-tenisa-praktyka-czyni-mistrza-wideo/5t6zmdf |language=pl |title=Robert Lewandowski pokazał, jak gra w tenisa. "Praktyka czyni mistrza" [Wideo] |website=Onet.pl |date=6 July 2022 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=30 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231030215659/https://przegladsportowy.onet.pl/ofsajd/robert-lewandowski-pokazal-jak-gra-w-tenisa-praktyka-czyni-mistrza-wideo/5t6zmdf |url-status=live }}</ref> He practiced playing tennis with [[Ana Ivanovic]], the wife of his friend [[Bastian Schweinsteiger]]<ref>{{Cite web |first=Janusz Przemysław|last=Gwizdek|url=https://sport.tvp.pl/61130692/aktywny-urlop-roberta-lewandowskiego-partia-tenisa-z-bastianem-schweinsteigerem-i-ana-ivanovic |language=pl |title=Aktywny urlop Roberta Lewandowskiego. Partia tenisa z Bastianem Schweinsteigerem i Aną Ivanović |website=TVP Sport|date=5 July 2022 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=9 April 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230409194254/https://sport.tvp.pl/61130692/aktywny-urlop-roberta-lewandowskiego-partia-tenisa-z-bastianem-schweinsteigerem-i-ana-ivanovic |url-status=live }}</ref> and personally knows [[Novak Djokovic]].<ref>{{Cite web |first=Rupin|last=Kale|url=https://www.sportskeeda.com/tennis/news-novak-djokovic-congratulates-robert-lewandowski-winning-champions-league |title=Novak Djokovic congratulates Robert Lewandowski for winning Champions League |website=sportskeeda.com |date=24 August 2020 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=26 September 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230926191928/https://www.sportskeeda.com/tennis/news-novak-djokovic-congratulates-robert-lewandowski-winning-champions-league |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |first=Robert|last=Czykiel|url=https://sportowefakty.wp.pl/pilka-nozna/896683/liga-mistrzow-robert-lewandowski-otrzymal-wyjatkowe-gratulacje-od-gwiazdy-tenisa |language=pl |title=Liga Mistrzów. Robert Lewandowski otrzymał wyjątkowe gratulacje od gwiazdy tenisa |website=sportowefakty.pl |date=24 August 2020 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=10 April 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230410114134/https://sportowefakty.wp.pl/pilka-nozna/896683/liga-mistrzow-robert-lewandowski-otrzymal-wyjatkowe-gratulacje-od-gwiazdy-tenisa |url-status=live }}</ref> He attended his matches in Qatar and United Arab Emirates.<ref>{{Cite web |first=Marcin|last=Motyka|url=https://sportowefakty.wp.pl/tenis/571581/robert-lewandowski-specjalnym-gosciem-na-meczu-novaka-djokovicia-z-rafaelem-nada |language=pl |title=Robert Lewandowski specjalnym gościem na meczu Novaka Djokovicia z Rafaelem Nadalem (foto) |website=sportowefakty.wp.pl|date=9 January 2016 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=26 September 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230926191928/https://sportowefakty.wp.pl/tenis/571581/robert-lewandowski-specjalnym-gosciem-na-meczu-novaka-djokovicia-z-rafaelem-nada |url-status=live }}</ref> In 2022, he personally congratulated [[Iga Świątek]] on winning the [[2022 Roland Garros]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.tennis.com/baseline/articles/robert-lewandowski-leads-congratulations-of-roland-garros-champ-iga-swiatek |first=David|last=Kane|title=Robert Lewandowski leads congratulations of Roland Garros champ Iga Swiatek |website=tennis.com|date=4 June 2022 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=26 September 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230926191928/https://www.tennis.com/baseline/articles/robert-lewandowski-leads-congratulations-of-roland-garros-champ-iga-swiatek |url-status=live }}</ref> He also plays [[golf]]<ref>{{Cite web |first=Robert|last=Czykiel|url=https://sportowefakty.wp.pl/pilka-nozna/820202/kocham-te-gre-robert-lewandowski-milosnikiem-golfa |language=pl |title="Kocham tę grę". Robert Lewandowski miłośnikiem golfa |website=sportowefakty.pl|date=7 May 2019 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=9 April 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230409143836/https://sportowefakty.wp.pl/pilka-nozna/820202/kocham-te-gre-robert-lewandowski-milosnikiem-golfa |url-status=live }}</ref> and is interested in motor sports, including [[Formula One]].<ref>{{Cite web |first=Janmeyjay|last=Shukla|url=https://thesportsrush.com/f1-news-fc-barcelona-star-striker-robert-lewandowski-biggest-inspiration-is-this-600-million-worth-formula-one-world-champion/ |title=Robert Lewandowski remembers 7-time world champion Michael Schumacher in F1 |website=thesportsrush.com|date=12 September 2022 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=26 September 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230926191930/https://thesportsrush.com/f1-news-fc-barcelona-star-striker-robert-lewandowski-biggest-inspiration-is-this-600-million-worth-formula-one-world-champion/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://sport.se.pl/pilka-nozna/bundesliga/robert-lewandowski-szaleje-na-mazurach-pedzi-na-skuterze-wodnym-wartym-krocie-zdjecie-aa-7zXn-NGwW-6jkb.html |language=pl |title=Robert Lewandowski szaleje na Mazurach! Pędzi na skuterze wodnym wartym krocie! [Zdjęcie] |website=sport.se.pl |date=8 July 2019 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=10 April 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230410102738/https://sport.se.pl/pilka-nozna/bundesliga/robert-lewandowski-szaleje-na-mazurach-pedzi-na-skuterze-wodnym-wartym-krocie-zdjecie-aa-7zXn-NGwW-6jkb.html |url-status=live }}</ref> In 2017 and 2022 as [[Aston Martin]] special guest, he attended the [[Monaco Grand Prix]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.polsatsport.pl/wiadomosc/2022-05-29/robert-lewandowski-pojawil-sie-na-grand-prix-monaco-polak-goscil-w-garazu-astona-martina/ |language=pl |title=Robert Lewandowski pojawił się na Grand Prix Monako. Polak gościł w garażu Astona Martina |website=Polsat Sport|date=29 May 2022 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=30 May 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230530081621/https://www.polsatsport.pl/wiadomosc/2022-05-29/robert-lewandowski-pojawil-sie-na-grand-prix-monaco-polak-goscil-w-garazu-astona-martina/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In 2023, he visited the paddock of [[Scuderia Ferrari]] during the [[Spanish Grand Prix]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://eurosport.tvn24.pl/formula-1/grand-prix-hiszpanii/2023/robert-lewandowski-z-wizyta-w-boksie-ferrari-przed-grand-prix-hiszpanii-2023_sto9640470/story.shtml |language=pl |title=Lewandowski Odwiedził Padok Ferrari Przed Grand Pris Hiszpanii|website=eurosport.tvn24.pl|publisher=TVN Poland|date=4 June 2023 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=5 June 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230605073623/https://eurosport.tvn24.pl/formula-1/grand-prix-hiszpanii/2023/robert-lewandowski-z-wizyta-w-boksie-ferrari-przed-grand-prix-hiszpanii-2023_sto9640470/story.shtml |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Philanthropy and business===

Lewandowski and his wife, Anna, have supported, donated and raised money for various charitable organisations and for children throughout their career, including [[Children's Memorial Health Institute]] in Warsaw, for which they've raised more than [[Polish złoty|PLN]] 150,000 during Anna's birthday party on 25 August 2018.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Halicki |first=Piotr |date=29 August 2018 |title=Wiemy, ile Lewandowscy zebrali na balu urodzinowym i na co pójdą pieniądze |language=pl |trans-title=We know, how much Lewandowscy raised at the birthday party and on what the money goes for |work=[[Onet.pl]] |publisher=[[Ringier#Joint Venture with Axel Springer in Eastern Europe|Ringier Axel Springer Polska]] |location=Warsaw |url=https://wiadomosci.onet.pl/kraj/wiemy-ile-lewandowscy-zebrali-na-balu-urodzinowym-i-na-co-pojda-pieniadze/5nv6ysp |access-date=5 June 2019 |archive-date=3 March 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210303154019/https://wiadomosci.onet.pl/kraj/wiemy-ile-lewandowscy-zebrali-na-balu-urodzinowym-i-na-co-pojda-pieniadze/5nv6ysp |url-status=live }}</ref> Lewandowski also donated PLN 100,000 for the treatment of Cyprian Gaweł, a three-year-old boy from [[Hel, Poland|Hel]];<ref>{{Cite news |date=11 December 2016 |title=Piękny gest Lewandowskiego. Przekazał 100 tys. zł na leczenie chorego chłopca |language=pl |trans-title=Beautiful gesture from Lewandowski. He donated 100 thousand zł for the ill boy's treatment |work=[[Onet.pl]] |publisher=[[Ringier#Joint Venture with Axel Springer in Eastern Europe|Ringier Axel Springer Polska]] |location=Warsaw |url=https://sport.onet.pl/ofsajd/faceci/piekny-gest-lewandowskiego-przekazal-100-tys-zl-na-leczenie-chorego-chlopca/2vkmt4 |access-date=5 June 2019 |archive-date=23 May 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210523203812/https://sport.onet.pl/ofsajd/faceci/piekny-gest-lewandowskiego-przekazal-100-tys-zl-na-leczenie-chorego-chlopca/2vkmt4 |url-status=live }}</ref> and helps raising funds for the [[Great Orchestra of Christmas Charity]] each year, donating his personal items or private meetings that are sold at online auctions.<ref>{{Cite news |date=9 January 2016 |title=Bilet VIP na Polaków, buty Lewandowskiego, trening z Jędrzejczyk. Sportowcy z WOŚP |language=pl |trans-title=VIP ticket for Poles, Lewandowski's boots, training with Jędrzejczyk. Sportspeople with WOŚP |work=Przegląd Sportowy |publisher=[[Ringier#Joint Venture with Axel Springer in Eastern Europe|Ringier Axel Springer Polska]] |location=Warsaw |url=https://www.przegladsportowy.pl/inne-dyscypliny/sportowcy-graja-z-24-wosp/wdesdcy |access-date=5 June 2019 |archive-date=23 May 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210523203815/https://www.przegladsportowy.pl/inne-dyscypliny/sportowcy-graja-z-24-wosp/wdesdcy |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Czekała |first=Filip |date=14 January 2018 |title=Lewandowski wystawił... siebie. Z 70 tysięcy klocków |language=pl |trans-title=Lewandowski listed... himself. From 70 thousand bricks |work=[[TVN24]] |publisher=[[TVN Group]] |location=Warsaw |url=https://www.tvn24.pl/wosp-2018/lewandowski-wystawil-siebie-z-70-tysiecy-klockow,805157.html |access-date=5 June 2019 |archive-date=5 June 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190605215306/https://www.tvn24.pl/wosp-2018/lewandowski-wystawil-siebie-z-70-tysiecy-klockow,805157.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Kubiak |first=Igor |date=24 January 2019 |title=Aukcja WOŚP: olbrzymie pieniądze za spotkanie i lunch z Robertem Lewandowskim |language=pl |trans-title=WOŚP auction: Huge money for meeting and lunch with Robert Lewandowski |work=[[Wirtualna Polska|WP SportoweFakty]] |location=Warsaw |url=https://sportowefakty.wp.pl/pilka-nozna/801117/aukcja-wosp-olbrzymie-pieniadze-za-spotkanie-i-lunch-z-robertem-lewandowskim |access-date=5 June 2019 |archive-date=23 May 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210523203812/https://sportowefakty.wp.pl/pilka-nozna/801117/aukcja-wosp-olbrzymie-pieniadze-za-spotkanie-i-lunch-z-robertem-lewandowskim |url-status=live }}</ref>

In March 2014, he was named a [[List of UNICEF Goodwill Ambassadors|UNICEF Goodwill Ambassador]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Goodwill Ambassadors & Advocates: National |url=https://www.unicef.org/people/people_nationalambassadors.html |access-date=5 June 2019 |publisher=[[UNICEF]] |archive-date=1 April 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190401033008/https://www.unicef.org/people/people_nationalambassadors.html |url-status=live }}</ref> In June the same year, he visited a refugee camp in [[Zaatari]], Jordan, and took part in the "Voice of the Children" campaign in which he appealed for support of children affected by humanitarian crises.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://przegladsportowy.onet.pl/pilka-nozna/reprezentacja-polski/nowa-misja-roberta-lewandowskiego-zostal-ambasadorem-dobrej-woli-unicef/stjv378 |language=pl |title=Nowa misja Roberta Lewandowskiego, został ambasadorem dobrej woli UNICEF |website=onet.pl |date=9 June 2014 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=26 September 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230926175505/https://przegladsportowy.onet.pl/pilka-nozna/reprezentacja-polski/nowa-misja-roberta-lewandowskiego-zostal-ambasadorem-dobrej-woli-unicef/stjv378 |url-status=live }}</ref>

In 2018, he and his wife donated PLN 500,000 to Children's Memorial Health Institute in Warsaw.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.sport.pl/inne/7,164769,23860342,anna-i-robert-lewandowscy-przekazali-ogromna-kwote-na-centrum.html |language=pl |title=Anna i Robert Lewandowscy przekazali ogromną kwotę na Centrum Zdrowia Dziecka. Para otworzyła klinikę rehabilitacji |website=sport.pl |date=4 September 2018 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=30 September 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220930031431/https://www.sport.pl/inne/7,164769,23860342,anna-i-robert-lewandowscy-przekazali-ogromna-kwote-na-centrum.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

In March 2020, Lewandowski and his wife, Anna, donated €1 million during the [[COVID-19 pandemic in Europe|COVID-19 pandemic]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Bayern Munich's Robert Lewandowski donates 1 million Euros to combat coronavirus pandemic |url=https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/bayern-munich-s-robert-lewandowski-donates-1-million-euro-combat-coronavirus-10642 |access-date=29 March 2020 |archive-date=23 May 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210523203813/https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/bayern-munich-s-robert-lewandowski-donates-1-million-euro-combat-coronavirus-10642 |url-status=live }}</ref>

In January 2022, he won a charity auction in which he paid PLN 280,000 for [[Dawid Tomala]]'s Olympic gold medal. The funds were used to finance the operation of a seriously ill boy.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://sport.tvp.pl/57870676/pilka-nozna-robert-lewandowski-wylicytowal-medal-dawida-tomali |language=pl |title=Jak powiedział, tak zrobił. Robert Lewandowski wylicytował medal Dawida Tomali |website=sport.tvp.pl |author=Sara Kalisz |date=9 January 2022 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=10 April 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230410145125/https://sport.tvp.pl/57870676/pilka-nozna-robert-lewandowski-wylicytowal-medal-dawida-tomali |url-status=live }}</ref> Lewandowski subsequently returned the medal to Tomala.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://sport.tvp.pl/59163891/robert-lewandowski-oddal-zloty-medal-olimpijski-dawidowi-tomali-musial-wrocic-do-wlasciciela |language=pl |title=Robert Lewandowski oddał złoty medal olimpijski Dawidowi Tomali. "Musiał wrócić do właściciela" |website=sport.tvp.pl |date=21 March 2022 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=26 September 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230926174433/https://sport.tvp.pl/59163891/robert-lewandowski-oddal-zloty-medal-olimpijski-dawidowi-tomali-musial-wrocic-do-wlasciciela |url-status=live }}</ref>

In February 2022, Lewandowski condemned the [[2022 Russian invasion of Ukraine|Russian invasion of Ukraine]] and showed his solidarity with the Ukrainian people by wearing a blue and yellow armband during a Bundesliga match.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.premierseason.com/bundesliga/lewandowski-sets-an-example-with-the-ukraine-captains-armband/ |title=Lewandowski sets an example with the Ukraine captain's armband |website=premierseason.com |author=Maria Keane |date=26 February 2022 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=30 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231030215700/https://www.premierseason.com/bundesliga/lewandowski-sets-an-example-with-the-ukraine-captains-armband/ |url-status=live }}</ref> The armband was later auctioned for PLN 27,000 and the money was used to purchase humanitarian aid for Ukraine.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://sport.interia.pl/robert-lewandowski/news-robert-lewandowski-przekazal-swoja-opaske-na-aukcje-zysk-z-l,nId,5873768 |language=pl |title=Robert Lewandowski przekazał swoją opaskę na aukcję. Zysk z licytacji pomoże Ukraińcom |website=interia.pl |author=Kamil Jagodyński |date=5 March 2022 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=10 April 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230410042043/https://sport.interia.pl/robert-lewandowski/news-robert-lewandowski-przekazal-swoja-opaske-na-aukcje-zysk-z-l,nId,5873768 |url-status=live }}</ref>

Beside philanthropy, Lewandowski also invests primarily in [[Startup company|startups]], [[e-commerce]], and websites, mainly through Protos Venture Capital, a company of which he is a shareholder.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Szewczak |first=Natalia |date=1 September 2017 |title=Biznesowa jedenastka Roberta Lewandowskiego. W co inwestuje polski piłkarz? |language=pl |trans-title=Robert Lewandowski's business eleven. What Polish footballer invests in? |work=[[Business Insider]] Polska |publisher=[[Ringier#Joint Venture with Axel Springer in Eastern Europe|Ringier Axel Springer Polska]] |location=Warsaw |url=https://businessinsider.com.pl/finanse/na-czym-zarabia-robert-lewandowski/tcvgyyq |access-date=5 June 2019 |archive-date=16 November 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181116063908/https://businessinsider.com.pl/finanse/na-czym-zarabia-robert-lewandowski/tcvgyyq |url-status=live }}</ref> He also owns Stor9_, an agency specialising in [[marketing communications]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Domaradzki |first=Krzysztof |date=21 June 2017 |title=Lewandowscy stawiają na marketing. Nowy biznes najlepszego polskiego piłkarza |language=pl |trans-title=Lewandowscy bet on marketing. New business of the best Polish footballer |work=[[Forbes]] |publisher=[[Ringier#Joint Venture with Axel Springer in Eastern Europe|Ringier Axel Springer Polska]] |location=Warsaw |url=https://www.forbes.pl/wiadomosci/stor9_-firma-roberta-lewandowskiego-marketing-roberta-i-anny-lewandowskich/pbfjs0y |access-date=5 June 2019 |archive-date=5 June 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190605215301/https://www.forbes.pl/wiadomosci/stor9_-firma-roberta-lewandowskiego-marketing-roberta-i-anny-lewandowskich/pbfjs0y |url-status=live }}</ref> In 2022, Lewandowski and his wife Anna's [[net worth]] was estimated at PLN 625 million (US$140 million), making them claim the 89th place on the "List of 100 Richest Poles" compiled by the ''[[Wprost]]'' magazine.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://i.pl/anna-i-robert-lewandowscy-na-liscie-najbogatszych-polakow-ich-majatek-robi-wrazenie/ar/c1-16458627 |language=pl |title=Anna i Robert Lewandowscy na liście najbogatszych Polaków. Ich majątek robi wrażenie |website=i.pl |author=Anna Piotrowska |date=28 June 2022 |access-date=28 September 2023 |archive-date=6 June 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230606234957/https://i.pl/anna-i-robert-lewandowscy-na-liscie-najbogatszych-polakow-ich-majatek-robi-wrazenie/ar/c1-16458627 |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Sponsorship and media appearances===
Since 2011 until 2018, he had a sponsorship contract with [[Gillette]] and appeared in numerous advertising campaigns of the brand.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.wirtualnemedia.pl/artykul/robert-lewandowski-w-kolejnej-kampanii-reklamowej-gillette |language=pl |title=Robert Lewandowski w kolejnej kampanii reklamowej Gillette |website=wirtualnemedia.pl |date=21 June 2016 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=21 July 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200721214333/https://www.wirtualnemedia.pl/artykul/robert-lewandowski-w-kolejnej-kampanii-reklamowej-gillette |url-status=live }}</ref> In 2020, the contract was renewed.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.wirtualnemedia.pl/artykul/robert-lewandowski-gillette-reklama-liga-mistrzow-w-tle |language=pl |title=Robert Lewandowski znów reklamuje Gillette, tym razem z Ligą Mistrzów w tle (wideo) |website=wirtualnemedia.pl |date=5 August 2020 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=17 February 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210217020401/https://www.wirtualnemedia.pl/artykul/robert-lewandowski-gillette-reklama-liga-mistrzow-w-tle |url-status=live }}</ref> In 2013, Lewandowski signed a sponsorship deal with [[Nike, Inc.|Nike]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=14 September 2021 |title=Robert Lewandowski – Sponsors &#124; Endorsements &#124; Salary &#124; Net Worth &#124; Notable Honours &#124; Charity Work |url=https://sportskhabri.com/player-profile-robert-lewandowski/ |access-date=20 July 2022 |website=SportsKhabri |language=en-US |archive-date=1 July 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220701164041/https://sportskhabri.com/player-profile-robert-lewandowski/ |url-status=live }}</ref> He also collaborated and appeared in advertisements of [[Panasonic]],<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.wirtualnemedia.pl/artykul/panasonic-poszerza-wspolprace-z-robertem-lewandowskim-o-marke-viera |language=pl |title=Panasonic poszerza współpracę z Robertem Lewandowskim o markę Viera |website=wirtualnemedia.pl |date=6 May 2014 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=26 September 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230926120853/https://www.wirtualnemedia.pl/artykul/panasonic-poszerza-wspolprace-z-robertem-lewandowskim-o-marke-viera |url-status=live }}</ref> [[T-Mobile Polska]],<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://android.com.pl/news/338539-robert-lewandowski-ambasadorem-t-mobile-polska/ |language=pl |title=Robert Lewandowski ambasadorem T-Mobile Polska – efekty współpracy już w tym miesiącu |website=android.com.pl |author=Mateusz nowak |date=14 August 2020 |access-date=26 September 2023 |archive-date=26 September 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230926120854/https://android.com.pl/news/338539-robert-lewandowski-ambasadorem-t-mobile-polska/ |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Coca-Cola]],<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.wirtualnemedia.pl/artykul/robert-lewandowski-zrezygnuje-z-reklam-marki-coca-cola-koniec-umowy |language=pl |title=Robert Lewandowski zakończył współpracę z marką Coca-Cola |website=wirtualnemedia.pl |author=Beata Goczał |date=10 January 2018 |access-date=26 September 2023}}</ref> [[Head & Shoulders]]<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.press.pl/tresc/43823,robert-lewandowski-ambasadorem-head-&-shoulders |language=pl |title=Robert Lewandowski ambasadorem Head & Shoulders |website=press.pl |author=Jakub Mejer |date=10 May 2016 |access-date=26 September 2023}}</ref> and [[4F (company)|4F]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://fashionbiznes.pl/robert-lewandowski-z-wizyta-w-4f-prezentuje-najnowsza-kolekcje-4fxrl9/ |title=Robert Lewandowski z wizytą w 4F prezentuje najnowszą kolekcję 4F×RL9 |website=fashionbiznes.pl |author=Magda Posełek |date=30 May 2022 |access-date=26 September 2023}}</ref>

In 2016, a mobile game ''Lewandowski: Euro Star 2016'' was released on [[Android (operating system)|Android]] and [[iOS]] platforms.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.dobreprogramy.pl/robert-lewandowski-ma-swoja-gre-mobilna-na-androida-oraz-ios-a,6628361433294977a |language=pl |title=Robert Lewandowski ma swoją grę mobilną na Androida oraz iOS-a |website=dobreprogramy.pl |author=Łukasz Maślanka |date=15 June 2016 |access-date=26 September 2023}}</ref>

In March 2022, Lewandowski cancelled his sponsorship deal with Chinese telecom company [[Huawei]] after the company's reported support to Russia following the Russian invasion of Ukraine. Lewandowski had signed on as the global ambassador for Huawei, after agreeing to a partnership in November 2015.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.mirror.co.uk/sport/football/news/lewandowski-sponsor-huawei-russia-ukraine-26406843|title=Robert Lewandowski drops sponsor Huawei in stand against Russia amid Ukraine attacks|last1=O'Brien|first1=Josh|last2=Blow|first2=Tom|newspaper=Daily Mirror|date=7 March 2022|access-date=8 March 2022}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://sportowefakty.wp.pl/pilka-nozna/988970/zdecydowana-reakcja-lewego-to-koniec-wspolpracy|title=Zdecydowana reakcja "Lewego". To koniec współpracy|newspaper=Sportowe Fakty|date=7 March 2022 |access-date=8 March 2022 |last1=Media |first1=Wirtualna Polska }}</ref>

Lewandowski featured on the cover of the Polish edition of EA Sports' ''[[FIFA 15]]'' video game, alongside [[Lionel Messi]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Kosman |first=Marcin |date=14 August 2014 |title=Robert Lewandowski na okładce FIFA 15, a Szpakowski i Szaranowicz na stanowisku komentatorskim |language=pl |trans-title=Robert Lewandowski on the cover of FIFA 15, with Szpakowski and Szaranowicz on commentary |work=Polygamia |url=http://polygamia.pl/Polygamia/1,107162,16476830,Robert_Lewandowski_na_okladce_FIFA_15__a_Szpakowski.html |access-date=3 July 2015 |archive-date=21 January 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160121212249/http://polygamia.pl/Polygamia/1,107162,16476830,Robert_Lewandowski_na_okladce_FIFA_15__a_Szpakowski.html |url-status=dead }}</ref> Lewandowski's "X" [[goal celebration]]—arms crossed and index fingers pointing up—has appeared in [[EA Sports]]' ''[[FIFA (video game series)|FIFA]]'' series since ''[[FIFA 18]]''.<ref>{{Cite news |title=How to do the 12 new FIFA 18 celebrations – plus more of our favourites |work=FourFourTwo |url=https://www.fourfourtwo.com/features/how-do-12-new-fifa-18-celebrations-plus-more-our-favourites |access-date=21 February 2022}}</ref>

In 2022, Lewandowski was the most popular Pole on [[social media]]. His accounts on [[Instagram]], [[YouTube]] and [[Tik Tok|TikTok]] were followed by over 62 million people.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://fashionbiznes.pl/10-najpopularniejszych-influencerow-2022-roku-ranking/#:~:text=Kto%20jest%20najpopularniejszym%20influencerem%20w%20Polsce%20w%202022%3F,jego%20wska%C5%BAnik%20popularno%C5%9Bci%2A%20wynosi%20aktualnie%20215%2C47%20mln%20z%C5%82. |language=pl |title=10 najpopularniejszych influencerów 2022 roku [ranking] |website=fashionbiznes.pl |author=Magda Posełek |date=28 March 2023 |access-date=26 September 2023}}</ref> In 2023, he was the subject of a [[documentary film]] entitled ''Lewandowski − Nieznany'' (Lewandowski − Unknown), which premiered on 28 March and is available on [[Amazon Prime]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.primevideo.com/detail/LEWANDOWSKI---UNKNOWN/0OL82U3P0LYHS6D9XVX5KPHHFL |title=LEWANDOWSKI - UNKNOWN |website=primevideo.com |access-date=26 September 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://sport.tvp.pl/68596055/kiedy-premiera-dokumentu-o-robercie-lewandowskim-amazon-opublikowal-trailer-lewandowski-nieznany-gdzie-ogladac |language=pl |title=Kiedy premiera dokumentu o Robercie Lewandowskim? Amazon opublikował trailer "Lewandowski Nieznany". Gdzie oglądać? |website=sport.tvp.pl |author=Maciej Rafalski |date=28 March 2023 |access-date=26 September 2023}}</ref>

